1
00:00:03,540 --> 00:02:03,540
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,085 --> 00:02:08,245
No animals were harmed during
the filming of this series.

3
00:02:08,645 --> 00:02:09,845
85th episode

4
00:02:09,905 --> 00:02:12,005
In the name of Mighty Allah...

5
00:02:12,365 --> 00:02:16,345
...who makes anything happen as he says...

6
00:02:16,615 --> 00:02:19,775
...and fills our hearts with faith.

7
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:24,485
In the name of Allah.

8
00:02:27,605 --> 00:02:31,275
Ordeal and difficulty.

9
00:02:33,315 --> 00:02:35,885
These are like valiant men.

10
00:02:37,935 --> 00:02:43,675
They never get close to those less
strong than them.

11
00:02:46,165 --> 00:02:48,375
They saw as equals...

12
00:02:49,345 --> 00:02:51,825
...so they never leave us alone.

13
00:02:53,515 --> 00:02:59,745
We survived many troubles, hardships.

14
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:04,325
But it is time...

15
00:03:05,975 --> 00:03:09,575
...to tell this tyrant to stop.

16
00:03:11,185 --> 00:03:13,075
Vizier Alemşah...

17
00:03:14,145 --> 00:03:15,725
...and Geyhatu.

18
00:03:17,325 --> 00:03:19,845
They are so cruel that...

19
00:03:21,185 --> 00:03:23,345
...they don't stop when you tell them.

20
00:03:25,345 --> 00:03:27,825
Now the way to stop them is...

21
00:03:30,985 --> 00:03:33,185
...the sword of justice.

22
00:03:37,625 --> 00:03:39,555
Their sentence is death.

23
00:03:40,085 --> 00:03:41,145
My Osman Bey...

24
00:03:41,565 --> 00:03:44,245
...the Vizier settled in Söğüt
as if it is his.

25
00:03:44,325 --> 00:03:45,905
Soldiers are everywhere.

26
00:03:46,055 --> 00:03:48,365
How can we take it back?

27
00:03:48,565 --> 00:03:50,205
Vizier can be managed.

28
00:03:50,375 --> 00:03:52,225
Söğüt is the property of Kayı.

29
00:03:52,365 --> 00:03:55,245
But how we will take Geyhatu...

30
00:03:55,425 --> 00:03:57,755
...from twenty thousand nökers...

31
00:03:57,805 --> 00:03:59,485
...my Bey?

32
00:04:00,275 --> 00:04:02,235
Only Söğüt?

33
00:04:04,245 --> 00:04:06,775
Who holds the far lands?

34
00:04:09,535 --> 00:04:10,835
You see...

35
00:04:11,255 --> 00:04:15,855
...they ride their horses on our property
without our permission!

36
00:04:18,075 --> 00:04:19,765
Before...

37
00:04:20,035 --> 00:04:21,894
...those nökers come...

38
00:04:22,285 --> 00:04:25,055
...we will hit them at their safest time.

39
00:04:27,395 --> 00:04:28,565
Master Davut...

40
00:04:29,475 --> 00:04:32,415
...how many swords have you
crafted so far?

41
00:04:32,755 --> 00:04:37,105
I crafted five for each valiant of
the tribe.

42
00:04:37,245 --> 00:04:40,005
Praise be!
Praise be!

43
00:04:42,485 --> 00:04:44,065
Akça Shepherd...

44
00:04:44,185 --> 00:04:45,545
...tell me...

45
00:04:45,745 --> 00:04:49,545
...how many jugs do we have to hit
the oppressor?

46
00:04:50,435 --> 00:04:52,075
Fifteen of them are ready, my Bey.

47
00:04:52,445 --> 00:04:57,085
I can make forty more if I will have time.

48
00:05:00,565 --> 00:05:02,375
Thank you.

49
00:05:04,165 --> 00:05:09,545
This is war.
People will die and get injured.

50
00:05:11,205 --> 00:05:12,325
Kumral Abdal...

51
00:05:12,965 --> 00:05:18,025
...do we have enough medicine, ointment
and bed?

52
00:05:19,745 --> 00:05:22,495
All of them are ready as you ordered,
my Bey.

53
00:05:25,225 --> 00:05:27,605
May Allah protect our alps!

54
00:05:27,695 --> 00:05:29,005
Amen!

55
00:05:29,075 --> 00:05:30,405
Amen!

56
00:05:30,475 --> 00:05:31,795
Amen!

57
00:05:31,805 --> 00:05:36,625
Measures and preparations are done.

58
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:44,975
But troubles will follow us.

59
00:05:46,805 --> 00:05:49,895
This won't end with Alemşah and
Geyhatu.

60
00:05:50,405 --> 00:05:57,845
I thought Alemşah did all these for his
own benefit.

61
00:05:59,035 --> 00:06:02,695
But he had another ally to his cruelty.

62
00:06:03,215 --> 00:06:04,755
Who is it, my Bey?

63
00:06:04,765 --> 00:06:06,105
Tell us, my Bey.

64
00:06:06,145 --> 00:06:08,035
Do you think of anyone, my Bey?

65
00:06:08,045 --> 00:06:10,835
Tell us, my Bey!

66
00:06:15,625 --> 00:06:18,595
Söğüt

67
00:06:18,950 --> 00:06:23,130
Rebellious Beys are with Osman Bey,
Vizier Alemşah.

68
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:29,440
Uğur Bey and his brother İvaz are also
on their way to the tribe.

69
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:33,400
İvaz's daughter is on her way too.

70
00:06:33,690 --> 00:06:37,560
In that case, we will be quick, Güngör.

71
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:43,550
We'll take the shepherd out and shoot
him before his flock grows.

72
00:06:46,730 --> 00:06:49,450
Loyalty is a rare quality.

73
00:06:49,970 --> 00:06:56,330
But the hardest thing is choosing to whom
you are loyal.

74
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:01,800
Since they chose Osman, they all will end
up the same.

75
00:07:02,390 --> 00:07:05,570
What are you planning, Vizier Alemşah.

76
00:07:06,350 --> 00:07:10,890
There is someone loyal to Osman
among us.

77
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:18,760
But if the traitor doesn't know
his betrayal is revealed...

78
00:07:20,290 --> 00:07:23,090
...he also won't know to whom he serves.

79
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:26,550
Erbey, call Konur!

80
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:34,020
Osman will be dead before İvaz arrives.

81
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:38,410
Now go. Traitor shouldn't see you.

82
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:41,710
Go and handle İvaz.

83
00:07:42,030 --> 00:07:44,430
All right, Vizier Alemşah.

84
00:07:44,770 --> 00:07:48,260
There will be no one left unhandled.

85
00:07:57,100 --> 00:08:01,650
You first handle your brother!

86
00:08:04,770 --> 00:08:06,970
You are no different from a dog!

87
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:09,740
Who can it be?

88
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:11,950
Is there anyone more degenerate
than Vizier?

89
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:13,430
Who is it, my Bey?

90
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:15,850
What does he get by working against us?

91
00:08:33,049 --> 00:08:35,308
We don't know who it is for now.

92
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:39,490
Sultan Mesud...

93
00:08:40,690 --> 00:08:43,150
... thinks that I tried to kill him.

94
00:08:47,090 --> 00:08:50,030
Before he believes this lie and
comes after me...

95
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:52,870
...I will find whoever did it and...

96
00:08:54,170 --> 00:08:56,050
...take care of it.

97
00:08:56,670 --> 00:08:58,080
My Bey...

98
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:00,750
...what should Kayı's beys do until then?

99
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:02,380
Order us, my Bey.

100
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:05,130
Start the war preparations.

101
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:08,190
Get armed.

102
00:09:09,170 --> 00:09:11,130
Alps must start the drills.

103
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:16,970
And train their children to become
a man.

104
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:19,070
As you order, my Bey!

105
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:21,550
We will get strong as a wolf, my Bey!

106
00:09:21,550 --> 00:09:24,790
No one can go against us now!

107
00:09:25,010 --> 00:09:26,010
Thank you.

108
00:09:26,630 --> 00:09:27,630
Thank you.

109
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:29,840
Only Kayı's beys, Osman Bey?

110
00:09:30,490 --> 00:09:34,410
Me, my alps and my tribe is always ready
to fight by your side.

111
00:09:34,530 --> 00:09:36,640
I know, Turgut Bey, I know.

112
00:09:39,510 --> 00:09:42,520
You have fought by my side
for a long time.

113
00:09:44,020 --> 00:09:45,470
But Beys...

114
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:48,780
...must listen to me before starting
the preparations.

115
00:09:53,290 --> 00:09:56,990
Alps' responsibility and order...

116
00:09:59,550 --> 00:10:01,390
...no longer belongs to Gündüz Bey.

117
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:10,670
Turgut Bey...

118
00:10:12,060 --> 00:10:13,910
...proved himself...

119
00:10:14,670 --> 00:10:16,450
...many times...

120
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:20,660
...in the plain of Konya and
at the Lord's Castle.

121
00:10:23,210 --> 00:10:30,610
Thus, he is now the head of the Alps
in Söğüt and in Kayı Tribe.

122
00:10:34,610 --> 00:10:37,030
As Osman Bey sees fit.

123
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,400
Thank you, Osman Bey.

124
00:10:50,170 --> 00:10:53,690
May my Rabb grant me the honor of
fulfilling this duty.

125
00:10:53,690 --> 00:10:56,790
-Amen! Amen!
-Amen! Amen!

126
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:58,440
I hope.

127
00:11:00,770 --> 00:11:04,140
Geyhatu lost breath while running from me.

128
00:11:05,280 --> 00:11:06,800
Now...

129
00:11:07,890 --> 00:11:11,480
...it is time for his last breath.

130
00:11:14,850 --> 00:11:19,550
Beys, you can start the preparations.

131
00:11:29,870 --> 00:11:31,710
You stay, brother.

132
00:11:43,170 --> 00:11:44,930
Come in, Konur.

133
00:11:48,210 --> 00:11:49,700
Yes, my Vizier?

134
00:11:51,010 --> 00:11:53,180
Osman is at his tribe.

135
00:11:54,470 --> 00:11:58,260
Did your spies lose their eyes, Konur?

136
00:12:02,390 --> 00:12:04,690
Reduce the number of soldiers.

137
00:12:06,250 --> 00:12:09,130
We won't be alone while raiding the tribe.

138
00:12:09,430 --> 00:12:11,300
We will go over the Wolf hill and...

139
00:12:11,570 --> 00:12:14,190
...secretly meet Geyhatu.

140
00:12:16,650 --> 00:12:18,350
As you order, my Vizier.

141
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:27,000
Erbey...

142
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:29,570
...go after this dog.

143
00:12:30,230 --> 00:12:33,940
Make sure he tells Osman about the plan.

144
00:12:34,090 --> 00:12:35,730
See it with your eyes.

145
00:12:36,970 --> 00:12:38,890
As you order, my Vizier.

146
00:12:44,950 --> 00:12:48,590
Fulfill your last duty to me, Konur.

147
00:12:50,150 --> 00:12:52,610
Lure Osman to my trap.

148
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,480
I promise you that...

149
00:12:57,600 --> 00:13:02,870
...I will hang you with Osman, to whom
you are loyal!

150
00:13:05,090 --> 00:13:06,690
Brother...

151
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:11,090
...do you resent me...

152
00:13:14,090 --> 00:13:15,670
...for taking your duty away?

153
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,420
No way, Osman Bey.

154
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:23,570
I have no right to resent.

155
00:13:27,210 --> 00:13:31,950
I have no goal other than helping you and
making up for my mistakes.

156
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,200
Thank you, brother.

157
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:37,010
Thank you.

158
00:13:38,870 --> 00:13:40,880
People make mistakes.

159
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:44,850
You are entrusted to me by my father
Ertuğrul Gazi.

160
00:13:46,790 --> 00:13:48,840
I entrusted you the tribe.

161
00:13:51,670 --> 00:13:53,310
But you made a mistake, brother.

162
00:13:56,530 --> 00:13:58,010
I know that...

163
00:13:59,450 --> 00:14:01,190
...your intention...

164
00:14:01,890 --> 00:14:08,170
...was to keep the tribe safe and
get the least harm you can get.

165
00:14:09,850 --> 00:14:11,570
Your intention was good.

166
00:14:13,090 --> 00:14:14,930
But your move was wrong.

167
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:21,060
You always want what's best for the tribe.

168
00:14:22,220 --> 00:14:24,050
But the best happens...

169
00:14:25,530 --> 00:14:27,770
...when you choose the right way, brother.

170
00:14:28,490 --> 00:14:29,970
Therefore...

171
00:14:32,230 --> 00:14:34,420
...I make you Kayı's Bookkeeper.

172
00:14:37,230 --> 00:14:38,490
Brother, Allah knows...

173
00:14:39,050 --> 00:14:43,380
...I would accept if you made me a
guardian at the door after what I've done.

174
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,830
Thank you, Osman Bey.

175
00:14:49,570 --> 00:14:51,170
Stay by my side...

176
00:14:52,730 --> 00:14:54,160
...support me...

177
00:14:54,350 --> 00:14:56,350
...open your eyes wide...

178
00:14:56,930 --> 00:14:58,950
...and we will fight together, brother.

179
00:14:59,330 --> 00:15:02,930
Your cause and way are of Allah.

180
00:15:03,320 --> 00:15:05,370
I am by your side, brother.

181
00:15:09,770 --> 00:15:11,950
You will glorify the tribe.

182
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:14,040
You will make new trade roads...

183
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,440
...new agreements.

184
00:15:18,020 --> 00:15:21,680
But you will do these without bowing...

185
00:15:22,570 --> 00:15:24,680
...without turning your back
on the people...

186
00:15:25,790 --> 00:15:30,310
...and without being deceived, brother.

187
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:35,780
I have full faith in you.

188
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:40,710
I will do whatever it takes to glorify our
tribe, brother.

189
00:15:40,890 --> 00:15:42,360
Believe me.

190
00:15:44,750 --> 00:15:46,050
Thank you.

191
00:16:22,390 --> 00:16:24,280
Hello, Akça Dervish.

192
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:27,390
Hello, Konuralp. Welcome.

193
00:16:34,540 --> 00:16:36,330
Inform Osman Bey at once.

194
00:16:38,220 --> 00:16:40,570
Don't worry, Konuralp.

195
00:16:42,030 --> 00:16:43,530
Be quick, Akça Dervish.

196
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,530
He needs to receive it immediately.

197
00:16:46,650 --> 00:16:48,170
Akça Dervish...

198
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:50,230
...be careful.

199
00:16:50,490 --> 00:16:52,500
Vizier's soldiers may watch you.

200
00:16:58,050 --> 00:17:00,080
May Allah help you, Osman Bey.

201
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:04,089
Konya Palace

202
00:17:06,550 --> 00:17:10,130
Vizier Alemşah told me to convey this
to you, my Sultan.

203
00:17:34,770 --> 00:17:41,290
As if it wasn't enough you tried to kill
Geyhatu and...

204
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:46,270
...inflicted Argun's wrath on you,
you also work with the Emperor, huh?

205
00:17:54,450 --> 00:17:57,890
You told me there were traitors.

206
00:17:59,110 --> 00:18:03,310
I almost believed you and forgot you tried
to kill me!

207
00:18:03,770 --> 00:18:06,260
There is no greater traitor than you,
Osman!

208
00:18:08,470 --> 00:18:10,890
We are going to the Kayı Tribe!

209
00:18:11,510 --> 00:18:12,710
As you order, my Sultan!

210
00:18:14,090 --> 00:18:15,730
Osman!

211
00:18:30,890 --> 00:18:33,000
Welcome, Konur.

212
00:18:37,990 --> 00:18:41,170
You should've sent our greetings
to Osman Bey.

213
00:18:55,130 --> 00:18:56,190
Konur!

214
00:18:58,610 --> 00:19:00,880
Now the truth is revealed!

215
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:10,310
Vizier Alemşah!

216
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:13,620
What does this mean?

217
00:19:13,990 --> 00:19:16,500
You know what it means better.

218
00:19:23,530 --> 00:19:27,190
You've disappointed me greatly, Konur.

219
00:19:30,090 --> 00:19:31,900
You traitor!

220
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:36,800
You went behind me looking into my eyes!

221
00:19:46,500 --> 00:19:47,620
You are the traitor!

222
00:19:50,030 --> 00:19:52,430
You work for yourself,
not for the State of Seljuk!

223
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:57,670
Thankfully I could see your true face!

224
00:19:59,350 --> 00:20:00,820
You, Vizer Alemşah...

225
00:20:03,090 --> 00:20:04,620
...are a hypocrite devil!

226
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:14,690
Loyalty is not easy.

227
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:20,810
But the hardest thing is choosing to whom
you are loyal.

228
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:32,820
You are a traitor Konur!

229
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:39,590
You worked with Osman and assassinated
the Sultan!

230
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:41,990
When I get Osman...

231
00:20:42,340 --> 00:20:47,950
...I will cut his head and send it
to Sultan with yours!

232
00:20:53,180 --> 00:20:55,960
Your treachery worked, Konur!

233
00:20:57,210 --> 00:21:01,490
Now I am luring Osman to a trap
thanks to you!

234
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:05,530
Speak, Alemşah, speak.

235
00:21:07,550 --> 00:21:09,580
You are the most despicable
of degenerates!

236
00:21:10,910 --> 00:21:13,090
You will pay for all you have done!

237
00:21:28,050 --> 00:21:30,050
Allah is the best of those who set a trap.

238
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:32,390
Throw this dog into the dungeon!

239
00:21:32,390 --> 00:21:35,050
He won't get a piece of bread,
a drop of water.

240
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:40,240
He should learn the price
for betraying the state!

241
00:21:41,420 --> 00:21:44,920
I didn't betray my state,
I served my state!

242
00:21:45,430 --> 00:21:47,880
That state is the state Osman Bey will
establish!

243
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:23,990
O Allah...

244
00:22:25,890 --> 00:22:27,890
...make my Aladdin Ali grow...

245
00:22:28,620 --> 00:22:33,620
...like a sapling in the garden of Islam.

246
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:40,790
May he be a valiant walking on the Islam's
road.

247
00:22:43,730 --> 00:22:44,990
My Rabb...

248
00:22:46,460 --> 00:22:52,630
...may you grant my Allaaddin Ali
a healthy and right life.

249
00:22:55,230 --> 00:22:56,770
Amen, my Osman.

250
00:22:57,520 --> 00:23:00,550
Son! Son!

251
00:23:23,590 --> 00:23:26,590
I wrote this when I found out
I was pregnant.

252
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:32,020
Ayatul Kursi.

253
00:23:37,620 --> 00:23:39,190
My Alaaddin Ali!

254
00:23:43,850 --> 00:23:46,960
What a beautiful name for my son.

255
00:23:53,210 --> 00:23:54,770
My wish is that...

256
00:23:55,510 --> 00:23:58,240
...you follow the right path like
Hazrat Ali.

257
00:24:00,810 --> 00:24:05,420
May you be a companion to your brother
Orhan.

258
00:24:07,960 --> 00:24:12,110
Don't ever hurt each other.

259
00:24:16,770 --> 00:24:19,230
Be a son worthy of your father Osman
Bey...

260
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:24,400
...and always be by your brother's side.

261
00:24:25,880 --> 00:24:29,530
What a great prayer, Bala.

262
00:24:31,260 --> 00:24:33,200
You have the heart of gold.

263
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:38,470
I already can see how a great son
you will raise.

264
00:24:50,130 --> 00:24:51,180
I wish that...

265
00:24:53,050 --> 00:24:57,010
...even if they are apart, their hearts
are still one.

266
00:24:57,730 --> 00:25:03,170
Alaaddin Ali, you have such a beautiful,
such a brave mother that...

267
00:25:07,160 --> 00:25:08,720
...you are so lucky.

268
00:25:11,660 --> 00:25:13,170
I hope...

269
00:25:14,370 --> 00:25:17,440
...you follow your grandfather
Sheik Edebalı's road.

270
00:25:21,990 --> 00:25:25,030
You will be the other light of our tribe,
son.

271
00:25:25,470 --> 00:25:28,010
Amen, my Osman.
I hope so.

272
00:25:28,980 --> 00:25:30,510
I hope so.

273
00:25:32,870 --> 00:25:34,950
Can I come in, my Bey?

274
00:25:37,200 --> 00:25:38,700
It is important, my Bey.

275
00:25:57,220 --> 00:25:58,590
Come in!

276
00:26:07,090 --> 00:26:08,420
My Bey...

277
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:12,610
...Akça Dervish brought this.
It is from Konur.

278
00:26:27,660 --> 00:26:29,230
Vizier!

279
00:26:31,230 --> 00:26:34,450
So you go to Geyhatu, huh?

280
00:26:36,170 --> 00:26:38,060
I will get you!

281
00:26:41,580 --> 00:26:43,290
It is time.

282
00:26:45,140 --> 00:26:46,680
We will hit the road.

283
00:26:47,930 --> 00:26:50,260
We will finish that Vizier.

284
00:26:52,330 --> 00:26:53,880
As you order, my Bey.

285
00:26:59,980 --> 00:27:02,790
Inegöl Castle

286
00:27:20,540 --> 00:27:25,480
Doesn't this ''Don't kill the messenger.''
phrase belong to the Turks?

287
00:27:44,150 --> 00:27:45,860
Then, what is this?

288
00:27:46,730 --> 00:27:48,280
What is this?

289
00:27:57,330 --> 00:27:58,850
That Vizier!

290
00:27:59,600 --> 00:28:02,320
He became such a barbarian after Geyhatu
but...

291
00:28:02,930 --> 00:28:05,660
...everything in this life has a price!

292
00:28:08,250 --> 00:28:10,020
If he didn't accept me...

293
00:28:11,450 --> 00:28:13,600
...if he is this brave...

294
00:28:14,280 --> 00:28:15,620
...all right.

295
00:28:16,050 --> 00:28:19,050
Then, I will set a new plan and...

296
00:28:19,050 --> 00:28:21,050
...deceive Osman.

297
00:28:22,950 --> 00:28:26,030
Karakus, prepare my horse.

298
00:28:26,570 --> 00:28:28,330
I am going to Kosses.

299
00:28:28,530 --> 00:28:30,290
To traitor Kosses!

300
00:28:30,510 --> 00:28:32,070
As you order, Sir.

301
00:29:20,750 --> 00:29:22,140
Stop!

302
00:29:30,910 --> 00:29:34,000
-Where are these good going?
-To the bazaar, my Bey.

303
00:29:35,830 --> 00:29:38,890
We are at war. You don't sell this much
goods when at war.

304
00:29:39,510 --> 00:29:42,180
What will people eat if the tribe
gets sieged?

305
00:29:42,300 --> 00:29:43,890
It is your order, my Bey.

306
00:29:43,890 --> 00:29:46,620
You told us to sell the goods before
waiting.

307
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:50,820
That time is over. Now, it is not about
money.

308
00:29:52,700 --> 00:29:55,030
It is about preparations, alps.

309
00:29:56,030 --> 00:29:57,340
Erdoğdu...

310
00:29:57,380 --> 00:30:00,990
...from now on, you will check every good
going to the bazaar.

311
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:04,490
Nothing will be on Kayı's stand before I
check it.

312
00:30:04,910 --> 00:30:06,450
As you order, my Bey.

313
00:30:06,610 --> 00:30:08,790
Come on. Return.

314
00:30:43,170 --> 00:30:45,170
-Check who it is.
-Yes, my Bey.

315
00:30:52,410 --> 00:30:53,740
Stop!

316
00:30:56,020 --> 00:30:57,340
Who are you?

317
00:30:57,420 --> 00:30:59,920
Selvi Hatun, İvaz Bey's daughter.

318
00:31:01,920 --> 00:31:05,740
Welcome, but we need to search
the carriage.

319
00:31:05,920 --> 00:31:06,940
For precaution.

320
00:31:09,630 --> 00:31:10,670
Alps!

321
00:31:17,010 --> 00:31:20,030
Selvi Hatun is Malhun Hatun's cousin.

322
00:31:20,520 --> 00:31:21,600
And our guest.

323
00:31:25,250 --> 00:31:27,750
-Don't keep her waiting.
-As you order, Gündüz Bey.

324
00:31:29,860 --> 00:31:33,200
-Welcome, Selvi Hatun.
-Thank you, Gündüz Bey.

325
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:37,060
Hatuns will accompany you to the tent.

326
00:31:37,510 --> 00:31:38,850
Thank you.

327
00:31:39,410 --> 00:31:40,720
Come in.

328
00:32:10,250 --> 00:32:12,950
Gee up! Gee up!

329
00:32:16,410 --> 00:32:17,720
Gee up!

330
00:32:18,630 --> 00:32:20,020
Gee up!

331
00:32:29,510 --> 00:32:31,280
Vizier Alemşah!

332
00:32:32,340 --> 00:32:34,900
The tyrant's time has run out!

333
00:32:35,800 --> 00:32:40,410
How do you know, Osman?
Does time belong to you?

334
00:32:41,490 --> 00:32:45,540
You are the one who lived longer
than he should.

335
00:32:46,530 --> 00:32:50,120
I will die for my dream, Alemşah!

336
00:32:50,740 --> 00:32:53,290
It will always stay as a dream, Osman.

337
00:32:54,500 --> 00:32:57,550
Because we are after the same goal.

338
00:32:59,740 --> 00:33:02,850
Two swords cannot fit in one scabbard.

339
00:33:07,150 --> 00:33:08,480
Erbey!

340
00:33:26,050 --> 00:33:27,630
Alps!

341
00:33:40,790 --> 00:33:43,050
Vizier!

342
00:33:54,760 --> 00:33:57,980
Osman Bey, this way!

343
00:34:06,050 --> 00:34:07,550
Come on!

344
00:34:07,760 --> 00:34:13,350
Alps! Come on!

345
00:34:23,520 --> 00:34:27,820
Go after them! Kill them all!
Come on! Come on!

346
00:34:29,250 --> 00:34:31,920
Osman will not leave here alive!

347
00:34:32,860 --> 00:34:35,330
Come on!

348
00:34:52,690 --> 00:34:54,960
Osman!

349
00:35:03,530 --> 00:35:05,810
Osman Bey!

350
00:35:15,250 --> 00:35:20,650
Valiants, follow me!

351
00:35:35,220 --> 00:35:39,450
Of course, our friends helped too.

352
00:36:23,760 --> 00:36:27,170
So you set a trap, Osman!

353
00:36:27,830 --> 00:36:34,850
What turns the dream into reality is
the idea that comes to mind...

354
00:36:38,710 --> 00:36:41,690
...to reach the heart.

355
00:36:41,890 --> 00:36:47,550
You set traps for us and we took measures.

356
00:36:49,580 --> 00:36:52,150
Thank you, Turgut Bey.

357
00:36:52,150 --> 00:36:53,860
Thank you.

358
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:58,710
Attack!

359
00:37:51,485 --> 00:37:54,885
Vizier!

360
00:38:16,685 --> 00:38:21,105
The punishment of the traitor is clear,
Konur. You did this to yourself.

361
00:38:23,985 --> 00:38:25,555
What kind of a man are you?

362
00:38:26,065 --> 00:38:28,355
Let's talk when my hands are untied.

363
00:38:29,050 --> 00:38:31,070
You betrayed the state!

364
00:38:31,520 --> 00:38:36,090
You worked with the rebel Osman.
You deserve worse!

365
00:38:40,890 --> 00:38:43,910
Do you do this because I deserve it
or because you are afraid?

366
00:38:43,950 --> 00:38:48,340
No one could save you from me if my
hands weren't tied.

367
00:38:48,440 --> 00:38:52,010
Do you think I am dumb, you traitor?
Are you trying to deceive me?

368
00:38:52,700 --> 00:38:55,200
I know what to do with you!

369
00:38:59,250 --> 00:39:01,550
I know what to do with you!

370
00:39:02,650 --> 00:39:08,250
You are dumb! So dumb that you believe
The Vizier's lies...

371
00:39:08,510 --> 00:39:11,660
...and turn your back on the truth!

372
00:39:53,385 --> 00:39:55,885
You have done so much.

373
00:40:00,085 --> 00:40:02,595
Not only to me.

374
00:40:05,085 --> 00:40:11,145
He intended to kill the hatuns of my tent.

375
00:40:31,335 --> 00:40:33,385
You spilled the blood of...

376
00:40:36,205 --> 00:40:39,475
...you spilled the blood of my mother.

377
00:40:42,675 --> 00:40:45,225
Vizier.

378
00:40:46,225 --> 00:40:48,815
Vizier.

379
00:40:53,040 --> 00:40:55,090
Come here!

380
00:40:55,120 --> 00:40:56,620
Come!

381
00:40:59,950 --> 00:41:06,520
You separated my son, my
Orhan from his mother.

382
00:41:29,975 --> 00:41:33,285
I haven't forgotten the
things you've done.

383
00:41:36,250 --> 00:41:40,130
You made Maria run away.

384
00:41:42,250 --> 00:41:45,330
Did you think you weren't
going to pay for all of this?

385
00:42:02,485 --> 00:42:07,305
I did all of that.
But did I do it all alone?

386
00:42:08,075 --> 00:42:11,595
Your brother was in on all of it.

387
00:42:14,225 --> 00:42:18,435
I know how you tricked my brother.

388
00:42:20,085 --> 00:42:22,325
I know his intentions.

389
00:42:24,395 --> 00:42:26,115
But,...

390
00:42:30,195 --> 00:42:33,965
...I will kill you with your own poison.

391
00:42:34,295 --> 00:42:37,025
If you don't kill me here...

392
00:42:39,495 --> 00:42:42,885
...I'll do worse, Osman.

393
00:42:47,335 --> 00:42:51,865
This time I won't separate
your child from his mother...

394
00:42:56,495 --> 00:42:59,715
...but I'll bury him in the ground.

395
00:43:01,675 --> 00:43:05,935
I'll kill you for that sentence alone.

396
00:43:16,315 --> 00:43:19,025
But you got things to say.

397
00:43:20,425 --> 00:43:24,935
You'll breathe until you say those things.

398
00:43:25,695 --> 00:43:30,915
Geyhatu will kill you
for doing these things.

399
00:43:33,095 --> 00:43:35,235
When he hears about it.

400
00:43:35,855 --> 00:43:37,615
Don't you worry at all.

401
00:43:39,595 --> 00:43:45,375
I'll get him too, thanks to you.

402
00:44:16,715 --> 00:44:18,975
Konur.

403
00:44:50,040 --> 00:44:52,540
You wait Selvi Hatun...

404
00:44:52,685 --> 00:44:55,255
...I'll inform Malhun Hatun.

405
00:45:04,385 --> 00:45:06,955
So this is where you live, Malhun.

406
00:45:20,385 --> 00:45:26,335
It's not enough being a mother, you also
want to be a khan for the government.

407
00:45:28,715 --> 00:45:34,045
You always set your sights high anyway,
the best tents of the tribe were always...

408
00:45:34,045 --> 00:45:35,045
...set up for you.

409
00:45:35,385 --> 00:45:38,475
The fastest horses were given to you.

410
00:45:50,685 --> 00:45:54,335
But all of that will change.

411
00:45:54,765 --> 00:45:57,845
I've had enough staying in
your shadow all this time.

412
00:45:59,115 --> 00:46:02,545
You'll see who is the
daughter of a bey, Malhun.

413
00:46:03,835 --> 00:46:10,745
Selvin, after the last moves Osman made,
these lands have gotten more dangerous.

414
00:46:11,045 --> 00:46:16,555
Don't worry, I'll end those
who are in my way.

415
00:46:18,105 --> 00:46:20,495
Watch Osman's tribe very carefully.

416
00:46:21,335 --> 00:46:23,355
Who is close to who...

417
00:46:23,415 --> 00:46:25,975
...or more importantly,
who is distant from who?

418
00:46:26,485 --> 00:46:28,715
Learn that well.

419
00:46:29,675 --> 00:46:34,125
We need to know where to break
those that are united like Kaya.

420
00:46:34,425 --> 00:46:39,995
Malhun is such an arrogant hatun that she
doesn't even see my hatred towards her.

421
00:46:40,305 --> 00:46:42,795
She doesn't even see
the rage I have against her.

422
00:46:43,245 --> 00:46:45,625
That's why she won't
hide anything from me.

423
00:46:45,715 --> 00:46:51,495
Selvi, don't let your rage
hinder your duty.

424
00:46:52,125 --> 00:46:55,765
You should go before for our goals.

425
00:46:56,965 --> 00:47:00,045
Watch the tribe and send me word.

426
00:47:00,095 --> 00:47:01,615
Don't have any worry, my bey.

427
00:47:02,355 --> 00:47:05,805
Malhun's life is always
at the edge of my dagger.

428
00:47:07,495 --> 00:47:10,845
There is no death before making
her suffer more than I had suffered.

429
00:47:13,655 --> 00:47:18,486
Don't worry about me,
come safely after me.

430
00:47:30,845 --> 00:47:32,365
Selvi sister!

431
00:47:34,665 --> 00:47:36,965
Malhun, sister!

432
00:47:37,445 --> 00:47:38,965
Welcome!

433
00:47:40,965 --> 00:47:42,765
Happy to be here sister!

434
00:47:43,165 --> 00:47:44,865
They're not worthy of you, but...

435
00:47:51,065 --> 00:47:52,595
...accept them.

436
00:47:52,595 --> 00:47:55,265
You shouldn't have, sister.
Thank you!

437
00:47:55,415 --> 00:47:58,365
Tell me, what brings you here?

438
00:47:58,965 --> 00:48:01,145
I want the good news, sister.

439
00:48:02,495 --> 00:48:06,615
My uncle Umur Bey is on the
way he'll be here by sunrise.

440
00:48:07,765 --> 00:48:10,815
After that Ivaz Bey will be here
along with the entire tent.

441
00:48:11,265 --> 00:48:12,995
We're together from now on, sister.

442
00:48:13,545 --> 00:48:15,145
What are you saying Selvi?

443
00:48:15,495 --> 00:48:17,595
Where is my father right now?

444
00:48:17,915 --> 00:48:19,815
On his way, sister, do not worry.

445
00:48:20,115 --> 00:48:24,315
Thank goodness!
Welcome back!

446
00:48:32,095 --> 00:48:33,945
ON THE WAY TO KERVANSARAY

447
00:48:33,945 --> 00:48:35,945
Umur Bey is like an uncle to me.

448
00:48:36,665 --> 00:48:41,515
Greet him very well innkeeper. Make sure
the table is flowing with milk and honey.

449
00:48:42,545 --> 00:48:46,195
The food and the drinks are ready.

450
00:48:46,665 --> 00:48:49,395
Everything has been done the
way you ordered, Barkın Bey.

451
00:48:50,265 --> 00:48:51,565
Good.

452
00:48:52,165 --> 00:48:56,065
Let's make sure it's a great service.

453
00:49:02,015 --> 00:49:04,515
He should have arrived by now, Hüsamettin.

454
00:49:04,520 --> 00:49:06,360
I'm sure he'll be here soon, my bey.

455
00:49:10,445 --> 00:49:12,445
My bey, Umur Bey is here.

456
00:49:18,695 --> 00:49:23,545
Umur Bey is a blessed man, Hüsamettin.
He came the moment we uttered his name.

457
00:49:24,415 --> 00:49:26,465
He won't let us miss him any longer.

458
00:49:30,295 --> 00:49:31,815
Umur Bey.

459
00:49:46,695 --> 00:49:50,065
Thank goodness, Umur Bey!
We've been waiting for you.

460
00:49:50,295 --> 00:49:53,445
- Welcome!
- Good to be here, Barkın!

461
00:50:05,765 --> 00:50:10,365
You will pay for what you've done, Osman.

462
00:50:15,115 --> 00:50:17,715
I got over my suffering, Vizier.

463
00:50:19,245 --> 00:50:24,915
Now, you will pay for the things
you've done, one by one.

464
00:50:26,545 --> 00:50:28,445
Now, wait here!

465
00:50:29,145 --> 00:50:34,245
That rope will be wrapped around
your and Geyhatu's neck.

466
00:50:36,015 --> 00:50:38,195
I'll take your reputation first...

467
00:50:40,595 --> 00:50:42,695
...then, your life.

468
00:50:52,465 --> 00:50:56,065
Konya will make you pay...

469
00:50:58,065 --> 00:51:01,595
...for what you've done
to Konya's Vizier, Osman.

470
00:51:07,795 --> 00:51:09,865
I welcome them, Vizier.

471
00:51:14,565 --> 00:51:16,365
I welcome them.

472
00:51:26,895 --> 00:51:29,615
Umur Bey, have you missed here?

473
00:51:29,715 --> 00:51:32,995
I even missed the air here.

474
00:51:33,795 --> 00:51:36,945
Even though I just came back...

475
00:51:37,845 --> 00:51:41,515
...I missed these sacred lands.

476
00:51:42,315 --> 00:51:44,095
The great Allah...

477
00:51:45,215 --> 00:51:49,565
...may he grant me to
see those lands again.

478
00:51:49,765 --> 00:51:51,215
If Allah permits, my bey.

479
00:52:00,725 --> 00:52:02,095
If Allah permits, my bey...

480
00:52:02,095 --> 00:52:06,165
...we'll pray at hajj together.

481
00:52:06,315 --> 00:52:07,605
If Allah permits.

482
00:52:08,695 --> 00:52:12,515
Nephew, where is Selvi?

483
00:52:12,965 --> 00:52:17,395
He wanted to go before me, Umur Bey.
She missed Malhun Hatun so much.

484
00:52:19,395 --> 00:52:20,565
Bless her.

485
00:52:20,995 --> 00:52:24,395
Turk's heart always leads.

486
00:52:24,895 --> 00:52:27,545
It doesn't suit them to stop, right?

487
00:52:29,945 --> 00:52:31,165
What do you think?

488
00:52:31,165 --> 00:52:35,295
What is it that brought us here?

489
00:52:50,645 --> 00:52:53,815
Fifty times stronger than the
ones that get stuck on wood.

490
00:52:54,415 --> 00:52:58,295
We'll tear Küffar limb from
limb if Allah permits.

491
00:52:58,665 --> 00:53:01,115
If Allah permits.
If Allah permits.

492
00:53:01,415 --> 00:53:03,415
Is this enough, Akça?

493
00:53:04,665 --> 00:53:06,245
Put plenty of it.

494
00:53:06,295 --> 00:53:09,595
Put plenty of iron so
that no tyrant is standing.

495
00:53:09,715 --> 00:53:11,045
Exactly!

496
00:53:11,865 --> 00:53:15,015
Put plenty of fire and iron.

497
00:53:16,615 --> 00:53:20,065
They didn't hold back their cruelty,
why should we hold back our rage?

498
00:53:21,115 --> 00:53:24,365
We'll do whatever our
conquest-loving heart wants.

499
00:53:25,345 --> 00:53:28,615
We'll spill their blood on these lands!

500
00:53:29,865 --> 00:53:33,945
These fires will burn our enemies good!

501
00:53:33,945 --> 00:53:36,715
May Allah bless you Kumral!

502
00:53:37,095 --> 00:53:41,315
All Muslims will unite!
All Turks will unite!

503
00:53:41,595 --> 00:53:45,865
Dervishes from one side,
sister warriors from the other!

504
00:53:46,265 --> 00:53:49,495
The alps from one side
soldiers from the other!

505
00:53:49,795 --> 00:53:54,665
We'll be the end of our enemies and the
hope of the oppressed if Allah permits!

506
00:53:55,065 --> 00:53:58,345
Allah Allah! Allah Allah!

507
00:53:58,345 --> 00:54:01,295
It's important to be the
hope of the oppressed.

508
00:54:02,015 --> 00:54:06,095
That comes with killing the tyrants.

509
00:54:07,865 --> 00:54:09,645
We will if Allah permits.

510
00:54:09,715 --> 00:54:13,145
Thank Allah who granted
with me comrades like you!

511
00:54:14,065 --> 00:54:15,565
Thank you all!

512
00:54:21,565 --> 00:54:25,695
The ones who have the same
goal become comrades, Raşid.

513
00:54:26,665 --> 00:54:30,345
Now, we'll keep the
promise we gave to Allah.

514
00:54:31,115 --> 00:54:32,945
The entire Muslim world will be one.

515
00:54:34,045 --> 00:54:39,565
The worshippers will
stand up to the tyrants!

516
00:54:42,365 --> 00:54:44,645
Our path, our cause is Islam!

517
00:54:44,915 --> 00:54:48,695
It is to spread Islam to the whole world!

518
00:54:49,195 --> 00:54:52,295
It is time to make the
tyrants get on their knees.

519
00:54:52,595 --> 00:54:56,365
It's time to make the
tyrants bow their heads.

520
00:54:56,715 --> 00:55:00,845
With the help of Allah,
we will defeat the tyrants!

521
00:55:01,415 --> 00:55:03,045
The worshippers...

522
00:55:04,045 --> 00:55:06,845
...you will achieve your
goals with Allah's help.

523
00:55:08,665 --> 00:55:09,795
Have no doubt.

524
00:55:09,795 --> 00:55:11,795
Allah is the greatest!

525
00:55:13,115 --> 00:55:14,695
It's almost over.

526
00:55:14,895 --> 00:55:17,615
Raşid, you get the horse carts ready.

527
00:55:18,145 --> 00:55:20,395
We're going to see Osman Bey!

528
00:55:20,395 --> 00:55:23,745
We're going to burn our enemies!

529
00:55:23,745 --> 00:55:27,245
Allah Allah! Allah Allah!

530
00:55:29,865 --> 00:55:31,195
May Allah bless you!

531
00:55:43,105 --> 00:55:46,635
It's the inland that makes these
lands important, Umur Bey.

532
00:55:48,155 --> 00:55:50,605
As horse trail gets mixed
up with dog trail...

533
00:55:51,645 --> 00:55:54,795
...The Turk's hope is draining away.

534
00:55:55,355 --> 00:55:58,865
- But...
- What but?

535
00:56:00,485 --> 00:56:02,235
We are fed by dreams.

536
00:56:04,555 --> 00:56:07,935
Loyalty cannot raise on this land.

537
00:56:09,255 --> 00:56:13,055
The essence of loyalty is order.

538
00:56:13,935 --> 00:56:16,985
Loyalty is nothing without order.

539
00:56:18,055 --> 00:56:24,485
Becomes stronger with the conscience
of the bey who is the head of the people.

540
00:56:25,605 --> 00:56:26,855
Umur Bey...

541
00:56:28,285 --> 00:56:32,905
...it seems easy to set up an order
when you're looking from far away.

542
00:56:33,185 --> 00:56:37,805
Even establishing a government seems easy.

543
00:56:39,235 --> 00:56:41,235
But I'm not so sure.

544
00:56:41,735 --> 00:56:43,035
So you say...

545
00:56:44,085 --> 00:56:48,955
...that Osman Bey is drinking
water from a river of dreams.

546
00:56:50,305 --> 00:56:55,535
Keeps drinking and not
getting fooled right?

547
00:56:56,005 --> 00:56:57,535
- Osman Bey...
- Shush!

548
00:57:01,505 --> 00:57:03,535
Tell me Ozan

549
00:57:05,155 --> 00:57:06,535
What did Osman Bey do?

550
00:57:06,705 --> 00:57:10,235
Osman Bey made the lands countries.

551
00:57:11,085 --> 00:57:12,855
His cause is our cause.

552
00:57:13,055 --> 00:57:16,735
The water he drinks is
from the rive of truth.

553
00:57:17,055 --> 00:57:18,405
Thank you!

554
00:57:19,235 --> 00:57:21,455
He is from Kayı Tribe.

555
00:57:22,835 --> 00:57:24,155
Thank you!

556
00:57:25,005 --> 00:57:28,555
He's been a friend to me for a long time.

557
00:57:37,485 --> 00:57:41,705
If you could just see uncle Umur,
he keeps talking about the Holy Land.

558
00:57:42,685 --> 00:57:44,305
He loved the Kaaba.

559
00:57:44,755 --> 00:57:48,985
He'll go back to the Hajj as soon
as he handles his business here.

560
00:57:50,955 --> 00:57:54,085
Who wouldn't want to see those holy lands.

561
00:57:54,335 --> 00:57:56,935
May Allah grant us with
that too if Allah permits.

562
00:57:57,085 --> 00:57:59,905
- Amen!
- Amen! If Allah permits, aunt.

563
00:58:05,505 --> 00:58:08,305
Malhun Hatun, are you well?

564
00:58:08,835 --> 00:58:10,485
You look faded.

565
00:58:11,335 --> 00:58:13,105
I'm well Ayşe Hatun.

566
00:58:13,655 --> 00:58:16,785
I felt strange when we
talked about my father.

567
00:58:19,685 --> 00:58:21,435
It's from excitement, my sister.

568
00:58:22,985 --> 00:58:28,715
Umur Bey kept talking about Osman
Bey's courage and about you.

569
00:58:30,055 --> 00:58:34,805
He says he won't be content if
he doesn't see Orhan before he dies.

570
00:58:34,885 --> 00:58:36,455
Allah forbid!

571
00:58:36,905 --> 00:58:39,805
- But he will see him if Allah permits.
- If Allah permits.

572
00:58:40,505 --> 00:58:41,835
If Allah permits.

573
00:58:49,805 --> 00:58:51,555
May I come in?

574
00:58:52,075 --> 00:58:53,955
Come in my girl.

575
00:58:56,815 --> 00:58:59,015
Bala, what's going on my girl?

576
00:58:59,015 --> 00:59:01,395
Why did you come back
this early from the tent?

577
00:59:01,665 --> 00:59:04,815
I can't sit at the tent all day mother.

578
00:59:06,065 --> 00:59:07,615
I'm well.

579
00:59:07,945 --> 00:59:10,015
Welcome Selvi Hatun!

580
00:59:10,065 --> 00:59:12,145
Happy to be here Bala Hatun!

581
00:59:12,475 --> 00:59:13,995
Sit, Bala.

582
00:59:22,045 --> 00:59:25,695
I've heard about your reputation
and about your beauty Bala Hatun.

583
00:59:27,265 --> 00:59:30,665
Praise be! You're even more
beautiful than what I've heard.

584
00:59:34,415 --> 00:59:38,045
I've heard from Malhun
that Orhan has a brother.

585
00:59:38,815 --> 00:59:41,815
May he be healthy.

586
00:59:42,165 --> 00:59:44,895
May he live long if Allah permits.

587
00:59:44,895 --> 00:59:46,215
Amen!

588
00:59:47,115 --> 00:59:49,695
- Amen!
- Thank you, Selvi Hatun!

589
00:59:53,845 --> 00:59:55,545
Look at Allah's work...

590
00:59:56,065 --> 00:59:59,715
...wait for all this time
and not have a child...

591
01:00:02,745 --> 01:00:06,465
My Creator's actions
are not questionable, daughter.

592
01:00:08,365 --> 01:00:10,095
So, tell us.

593
01:00:10,515 --> 01:00:12,845
Who is your fiancee?

594
01:00:12,845 --> 01:00:16,645
Your father Ivaz Bey wouldn't see
anyone suitable for you.

595
01:00:16,645 --> 01:00:19,195
How did he permit?

596
01:00:20,165 --> 01:00:22,195
Barkın Bey is from our tribe,
Selcan Hatun.

597
01:00:23,145 --> 01:00:28,465
He is beloved in the tribe.
He is so warm and lovely.

598
01:00:30,465 --> 01:00:34,065
When the tribe loved him,
my father's thoughts changed.

599
01:00:34,165 --> 01:00:35,345
He was convinced.

600
01:00:48,195 --> 01:00:52,895
Loyalty is appropriate when there are
Beys like Osman.

601
01:00:53,595 --> 01:00:57,265
Then you can build the order
and the state.

602
01:00:58,165 --> 01:00:59,665
Wrong!

603
01:01:03,295 --> 01:01:05,095
Kill them all!

604
01:01:05,095 --> 01:01:08,295
Order is corrupted!

605
01:01:08,295 --> 01:01:12,865
Fear exhausts our souls.

606
01:01:12,865 --> 01:01:16,195
- You will fear!
- Shut up!

607
01:01:17,165 --> 01:01:20,915
Damn the day we accepted you
in our tribe!

608
01:01:31,795 --> 01:01:34,495
Harmankaya Castle

609
01:01:38,050 --> 01:01:42,050
You are one of the most royal Lords
this lands will witness.

610
01:01:51,570 --> 01:01:55,930
Aya Nicola.
Are you that desperate?

611
01:01:58,370 --> 01:01:59,670
Friend, huh.

612
01:02:00,630 --> 01:02:03,710
Your only friend is your interests.

613
01:02:06,030 --> 01:02:08,110
You don't need to play with me.

614
01:02:08,870 --> 01:02:11,830
I read your mind word by word.

615
01:02:16,830 --> 01:02:18,210
Now that you can read...

616
01:02:18,210 --> 01:02:23,810
...you should see that I am happy to
be ally with you and even Osman Bey.

617
01:02:24,290 --> 01:02:26,310
I see, Nikola.

618
01:02:27,290 --> 01:02:32,770
Unfortunetaly, when I look at you, the only
thing I see is a devil in disguise.

619
01:02:34,550 --> 01:02:38,410
Okay, Kosses, if it was not for
those devils, it would be boring...

620
01:02:38,410 --> 01:02:40,530
War, war, war and more war!

621
01:02:40,610 --> 01:02:44,650
Also, I don't think Osman Bey prejudges
as much as you do.

622
01:02:44,810 --> 01:02:50,830
Although we have been enemies for years,
I think he is happy to ally with me.

623
01:02:50,830 --> 01:02:52,830
Osman Bey trusts me.

624
01:02:53,050 --> 01:02:54,630
Doesn't he?

625
01:03:00,250 --> 01:03:04,430
Speaks Latin
Nikola.

626
01:03:05,190 --> 01:03:07,090
Trust causes trust.

627
01:03:15,470 --> 01:03:21,810
Osman trusts you as much as you
trust Osman.

628
01:03:24,430 --> 01:03:28,090
No more, no less.

629
01:03:33,530 --> 01:03:35,270
Not everyone is like Samuel.

630
01:03:36,650 --> 01:03:40,770
He made sure of our trust
even when he was at the opponent's side.

631
01:03:55,030 --> 01:03:57,070
Allow us, Lord Kosses.

632
01:03:57,110 --> 01:03:58,830
News from Osman Bey!

633
01:03:58,870 --> 01:04:00,370
Come in Kyros!

634
01:04:05,510 --> 01:04:07,550
Osman Bey's alp arrived, sir.

635
01:04:07,610 --> 01:04:09,670
Osman Bey invites you to his tent.

636
01:04:11,750 --> 01:04:13,890
He wants Lord Nikola as well.

637
01:04:16,530 --> 01:04:17,870
Me?

638
01:04:17,870 --> 01:04:19,990
Of course, with pleasure.

639
01:04:23,650 --> 01:04:24,730
Right, my dear friend?

640
01:04:25,770 --> 01:04:27,390
Not without you.

641
01:04:31,470 --> 01:04:34,490
Prepare the horses.
Let's not keep Osman Bey waiting.

642
01:04:54,910 --> 01:04:56,530
I told you Mingeon.

643
01:04:57,290 --> 01:04:59,850
Vizier Alamshah has the control of
Osman now.

644
01:05:00,350 --> 01:05:03,350
Geyhatu has been waiting for this moment
for a long time.

645
01:05:03,610 --> 01:05:06,130
He will not kill Osman easily.

646
01:05:07,490 --> 01:05:10,110
Osman! Osman!

647
01:05:14,870 --> 01:05:16,570
Osmannnnnn!

648
01:05:16,570 --> 01:05:18,150
Come again!

649
01:05:18,750 --> 01:05:20,290
Osmannnn!

650
01:05:27,350 --> 01:05:28,790
Osman.

651
01:05:29,190 --> 01:05:31,210
Ya Osman!!

652
01:05:50,090 --> 01:05:52,310
Loyalty starts with fear...

653
01:05:52,310 --> 01:05:53,810
...grows with order!

654
01:05:54,890 --> 01:05:56,930
I'll make these lands fear me!

655
01:05:57,010 --> 01:06:01,510
Only cowards fear!

656
01:06:02,250 --> 01:06:07,530
I am an old man.
Don't you know that...

657
01:06:08,490 --> 01:06:12,150
...you can't fear an old Alp
with sword!

658
01:06:13,810 --> 01:06:18,510
Come at me, Barkin!
Come at me!

659
01:06:19,010 --> 01:06:21,330
Fear lets one stay alive.

660
01:06:27,110 --> 01:06:31,270
The one who is afraid can do
anything to live.

661
01:06:36,990 --> 01:06:38,370
Look.

662
01:06:38,990 --> 01:06:40,330
How fearful they are!

663
01:06:43,150 --> 01:06:46,730
If they weren't afraid, they might have
escaped while I was busy with you.

664
01:07:05,210 --> 01:07:06,510
Sister.

665
01:07:07,410 --> 01:07:09,430
Is there something wrong in the tribe?

666
01:07:09,490 --> 01:07:11,230
Alps are everywhere.

667
01:07:11,830 --> 01:07:13,910
They searched the carriage too.

668
01:07:14,510 --> 01:07:16,570
Our tribe is under threats, daughter.

669
01:07:17,890 --> 01:07:20,930
A rose garden contains many thorns.

670
01:07:22,010 --> 01:07:23,790
We have lots of trouble.

671
01:07:23,830 --> 01:07:26,350
Sometiems Lords, sometimes Mongols.

672
01:07:27,450 --> 01:07:30,050
And that Alemshah!

673
01:07:30,970 --> 01:07:32,770
He nearly set us against each other!

674
01:07:33,730 --> 01:07:36,630
Thank Allah you came just in time,
Selvi Hatun.

675
01:07:37,630 --> 01:07:39,770
Osman Bey went to call them to account.

676
01:07:42,450 --> 01:07:44,310
Tell us, how is it like
in your lands?

677
01:07:44,430 --> 01:07:46,310
How many tents will you bring?

678
01:07:47,230 --> 01:07:49,810
Our tribe has 500 tents, Selcan Hatun.

679
01:07:49,870 --> 01:07:52,570
We have 1000 cavalries with old men
and young men.

680
01:07:54,470 --> 01:07:55,990
Good, good.

681
01:07:59,050 --> 01:08:00,830
Our lands are like as you know.

682
01:08:01,570 --> 01:08:03,090
Troubled as always.

683
01:08:03,770 --> 01:08:05,890
Our lands need valiants.

684
01:08:05,990 --> 01:08:08,950
We need valiant hatuns like you.

685
01:08:09,330 --> 01:08:13,190
Ivaz Bey's arrival will strengthen
the whole Turkmen tribes!

686
01:08:13,790 --> 01:08:15,310
Inshallah. (If Allah permits)

687
01:09:27,229 --> 01:09:28,729
Barkin Bey!

688
01:09:28,950 --> 01:09:31,029
Every alp died from Kizilbeyogullari.

689
01:09:32,450 --> 01:09:35,069
We killed our alps who disobeyed as well.

690
01:09:35,229 --> 01:09:38,270
Whoever disobeys my commands
are not my alps anymore!

691
01:09:44,569 --> 01:09:45,910
My valiants!

692
01:09:47,649 --> 01:09:49,470
Why did you kill my alps!

693
01:09:50,910 --> 01:09:55,190
Not your alps, think about yourself,
Umur Bey.

694
01:10:19,230 --> 01:10:20,770
Umur Bey.

695
01:10:22,510 --> 01:10:25,070
He is a valiant man.

696
01:10:26,350 --> 01:10:28,130
You've seen it, didn't you?

697
01:10:29,150 --> 01:10:32,030
How I slaughtered the Mongol dogs!

698
01:10:34,450 --> 01:10:35,770
Traitor!

699
01:10:38,100 --> 01:10:44,040
Why did you kill my
valiants?

700
01:10:45,930 --> 01:10:48,110
Do you hear what he says?

701
01:10:53,170 --> 01:11:00,020
He says "my daughter Malhun".
He salutes her.

702
01:11:03,790 --> 01:11:04,910
Orhan?

703
01:11:07,310 --> 01:11:14,310
That one you kept talking about even
though you've never seen?

704
01:11:16,230 --> 01:11:19,470
He says hug my Orhan for me.

705
01:11:20,600 --> 01:11:22,050
He says, "smell him".

706
01:11:23,190 --> 01:11:24,630
Sure, Umur Bey.

707
01:11:25,670 --> 01:11:27,650
I'll hug your...

708
01:11:29,050 --> 01:11:31,230
grandson for you...

709
01:11:34,250 --> 01:11:36,330
tightly...

710
01:11:37,650 --> 01:11:39,490
tightly...

711
01:11:43,330 --> 01:11:46,000
Orhan!

712
01:12:26,310 --> 01:12:28,350
My father-in-law...

713
01:12:29,110 --> 01:12:31,330
will share the same fate.

714
01:12:32,610 --> 01:12:34,470
Come on.

715
01:13:08,150 --> 01:13:09,530
Umur!

716
01:13:09,810 --> 01:13:11,130
Ihvaz!

717
01:13:11,410 --> 01:13:12,710
Osman!

718
01:13:13,710 --> 01:13:18,150
They are talking about order and unity!

719
01:13:19,370 --> 01:13:20,950
But they don't know...

720
01:13:21,790 --> 01:13:24,830
unity comes from chaos!

721
01:13:26,230 --> 01:13:28,030
I'll burn the borders...

722
01:13:28,750 --> 01:13:31,930
I'll break their walls...

723
01:13:33,330 --> 01:13:36,330
they'll have no chance but
to join me.

724
01:13:38,090 --> 01:13:45,910
We won't leave our future
to dreamers.

725
01:13:46,550 --> 01:13:48,070
I'll rule with fear...

726
01:13:49,090 --> 01:13:51,070
and might!

727
01:13:54,030 --> 01:13:55,410
Brothers!

728
01:13:55,590 --> 01:13:58,830
Ihvaz Bey will share the same
fate with Umur Bey.

729
01:13:59,730 --> 01:14:01,030
And Osman.

730
01:14:01,870 --> 01:14:20,370
Long live Barkın Bey!
Long live Barkın Bey!

731
01:14:22,450 --> 01:14:24,010
Hüsamettin.

732
01:14:27,230 --> 01:14:29,250
This is our quarters now.

733
01:14:30,450 --> 01:14:32,170
Prepare it.

734
01:14:45,890 --> 01:14:47,670
What are you doing here?

735
01:14:47,870 --> 01:14:49,460
We'll blow it up.

736
01:14:49,585 --> 01:15:04,585
Brought to you by historicalfuntv.com

737
01:15:06,475 --> 01:15:11,905
Finally, I made you kneel.

738
01:15:13,745 --> 01:15:18,965
You'll face the most painful death, Osman.

739
01:15:20,485 --> 01:15:26,925
You'll face infinite suffering in hell.

740
01:15:29,085 --> 01:15:31,355
I'll skin you alive...

741
01:15:31,635 --> 01:15:37,125
I'll send your parts to rebellious beys.

742
01:15:38,585 --> 01:15:41,585
I'll be an example.

743
01:15:42,015 --> 01:15:50,865
But the Kayı; Gündüz's betrayal,
your insolence...

744
01:15:52,215 --> 01:15:54,975
I'll destroy the Kayı.

745
01:15:57,655 --> 01:16:02,175
I'll cause your extinction, Osman.

746
01:16:02,985 --> 01:16:06,055
Gündüz Bey is detoxicated.

747
01:16:07,905 --> 01:16:10,475
Don't hold back.

748
01:16:11,915 --> 01:16:18,995
Even if we are no more, someone
will hold the flag of Islam.

749
01:16:20,785 --> 01:16:27,925
But you won't die before the plots
you built with that vizier.

750
01:16:28,925 --> 01:16:34,175
I will kill you with my own hands.

751
01:16:37,905 --> 01:16:40,475
Stubborn Turk.

752
01:16:42,965 --> 01:16:46,675
Speak like this when I skin you alive.

753
01:16:46,975 --> 01:16:55,985
I'll kill your inheritor and you,
just like this.

754
01:17:07,045 --> 01:17:11,475
I'll cut your face first.

755
01:17:13,455 --> 01:17:16,265
Like Bilāl ibn Rabāḥ...

756
01:17:17,055 --> 01:17:20,295
we only serve Allah.

757
01:17:21,925 --> 01:17:25,355
Even if your tyranny rises to the sky...

758
01:17:26,495 --> 01:17:29,195
it can never stop us.

759
01:17:33,175 --> 01:17:36,015
Allah is good!

760
01:17:36,015 --> 01:17:38,195
-Allah is righteous!
-Allah is righteous!

761
01:17:52,135 --> 01:17:55,525
Geyhatu, I have you now.

762
01:17:55,925 --> 01:17:59,985
I'll put you and Vizier Alemşah
in a cage.

763
01:18:04,965 --> 01:18:07,965
If you kill me,
Argun will come.

764
01:18:08,025 --> 01:18:16,455
Then, forget the Kayı, not a single
Turk or Muslim survives.

765
01:18:16,515 --> 01:18:25,165
Forget Argun Khan, even if Kubilai Khan
comes from Hanbalık, he can't save you.

766
01:18:25,845 --> 01:18:27,425
Alps!

767
01:18:30,475 --> 01:18:32,315
Bury the dead.

768
01:18:32,775 --> 01:18:34,805
Take the wounded as captives.

769
01:18:36,075 --> 01:18:39,535
Share the horses and weapons.

770
01:18:56,525 --> 01:18:57,845
Wait!

771
01:19:11,785 --> 01:19:14,535
The best archer I have.

772
01:19:15,435 --> 01:19:20,515
Before my enemy releases a single arrow,
you shoot three.

773
01:19:21,005 --> 01:19:22,315
But...

774
01:19:22,895 --> 01:19:25,465
is your tongue as tense as your bow?

775
01:19:29,225 --> 01:19:31,295
You know my secrets.

776
01:19:32,065 --> 01:19:33,445
Don't you?

777
01:19:34,365 --> 01:19:35,935
Yes, my bey.

778
01:19:38,485 --> 01:19:40,025
This is bad.

779
01:19:41,535 --> 01:19:42,915
Bad.

780
01:19:44,165 --> 01:19:49,595
My secrets are too heavy for
you to carry.

781
01:19:55,195 --> 01:20:00,125
You shouldn't have learned them.

782
01:20:01,555 --> 01:20:05,935
You shouldn't have.

783
01:20:06,345 --> 01:20:08,235
Now, whatever you know...

784
01:20:09,485 --> 01:20:11,995
it will go to the grave.

785
01:20:35,725 --> 01:20:39,185
A wolf that can get into
a herd alone.

786
01:20:40,805 --> 01:20:44,815
Tell me, what are my goals?

787
01:20:45,055 --> 01:20:47,055
Breaking the order that is built, my bey.

788
01:20:52,115 --> 01:20:55,985
One who knows my goal,
knows my secret.

789
01:20:59,805 --> 01:21:04,665
I said it. My secrets are heavy.

790
01:21:17,245 --> 01:21:19,685
My bey's tent is this way.

791
01:21:21,005 --> 01:21:23,415
The tent of the brothers is
this way.

792
01:21:27,445 --> 01:21:30,965
Then, the white tent will be far.

793
01:21:32,045 --> 01:21:34,235
If I set it here...

794
01:21:35,565 --> 01:21:37,275
it will be far from my bey's.

795
01:21:40,375 --> 01:21:42,515
Allah Allah!

796
01:21:55,195 --> 01:21:56,495
Cerkutay!

797
01:21:57,385 --> 01:22:01,015
Cerkutay, why are you wandering
around like crazy?

798
01:22:01,505 --> 01:22:03,695
You are wounded.

799
01:22:04,125 --> 01:22:05,665
Have you forgotten about it?

800
01:22:06,265 --> 01:22:08,885
I haven't, my wife.

801
01:22:10,425 --> 01:22:11,675
I haven't.

802
01:22:12,215 --> 01:22:14,785
I'm thinking where to set our
tent.

803
01:22:14,975 --> 01:22:17,215
I was going to call you
when I see a place.

804
01:22:17,325 --> 01:22:21,845
-Why are you thinking? Just do it.
-No. It's important.

805
01:22:22,085 --> 01:22:24,335
It's very important.

806
01:22:26,985 --> 01:22:28,725
Let me think a little longer.

807
01:22:38,545 --> 01:22:40,275
Don't think, Cerkutay.

808
01:22:40,295 --> 01:22:44,435
Close your eyes. Shoot it.
And let's be done with it.

809
01:22:46,865 --> 01:22:48,395
I should?

810
01:22:48,435 --> 01:22:49,785
Do it.

811
01:23:01,795 --> 01:23:03,505
I should think.

812
01:23:04,185 --> 01:23:06,215
Let me think.

813
01:23:19,705 --> 01:23:22,525
I wanted you to shoot it.

814
01:23:26,065 --> 01:23:27,395
Come on.

815
01:23:29,065 --> 01:23:30,775
Go and set our home.

816
01:23:31,075 --> 01:23:35,775
I'll accompany Malhun Hatun and
Özge Hatun.

817
01:23:38,435 --> 01:23:40,005
I'll set it?

818
01:23:40,025 --> 01:23:43,545
How can I set it like this, mad girl?

819
01:23:43,785 --> 01:23:45,085
She is mad!

820
01:23:45,355 --> 01:23:46,915
And the home...

821
01:23:51,575 --> 01:23:56,175
Cerkutay will build it.

822
01:23:59,935 --> 01:24:02,125
They had a use...

823
01:24:02,535 --> 01:24:04,035
Hüsamettin.

824
01:24:12,025 --> 01:24:14,075
What are you proud of?

825
01:24:14,705 --> 01:24:16,225
Of my loyalty.

826
01:24:17,515 --> 01:24:19,655
I'm proud of my loyalty, my bey.

827
01:24:20,795 --> 01:24:22,715
Why did these men die?

828
01:24:23,985 --> 01:24:31,155
You killed them for me to understand how
valuable I am as a loyal man.

829
01:24:31,585 --> 01:24:34,565
These valiants who fought
alongside me for years...

830
01:24:35,485 --> 01:24:38,375
maybe they would never
betray me.

831
01:24:39,105 --> 01:24:42,275
But I killed them for you, Hüsamettin.

832
01:24:43,135 --> 01:24:44,765
You can be loyal.

833
01:24:45,405 --> 01:24:49,845
Don't forget what will happen to
you if you go astray.

834
01:24:50,255 --> 01:24:52,305
Never forget this.

835
01:25:13,435 --> 01:25:28,535
Osman Bey is coming!
Osman Bey is coming!

836
01:25:32,965 --> 01:25:34,965
Welcome, my bey!

837
01:25:35,295 --> 01:25:37,895
Welcome, Osman Bey!

838
01:26:24,555 --> 01:26:28,505
Osman Bey, we thank Allah for you!

839
01:26:28,725 --> 01:26:31,045
His soldiers killed my husband.

840
01:26:31,185 --> 01:26:34,805
May Allah bless you for bringing
him like this.

841
01:26:37,295 --> 01:26:40,275
It's the responsibility of a man
who is after justice.

842
01:26:41,865 --> 01:26:43,415
Thank you.

843
01:27:25,695 --> 01:27:30,885
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

844
01:27:31,155 --> 01:27:46,705
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

845
01:27:47,850 --> 01:28:07,850
Brought to you by historicalfuntv.com

846
01:28:09,350 --> 01:28:21,480
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

847
01:28:57,685 --> 01:28:59,415
What did Osman Bey do?

848
01:28:59,415 --> 01:29:01,735
He equipped the sword of justice!

849
01:29:01,735 --> 01:29:03,735
What did Osman Bey do?

850
01:29:03,745 --> 01:29:06,385
He protected the oppressed!

851
01:29:06,615 --> 01:29:08,655
What did Osman Bey do?

852
01:29:08,695 --> 01:29:11,325
He made the tyrants kneel!

853
01:29:11,325 --> 01:29:13,095
What did Osman Bey do?

854
01:29:13,095 --> 01:29:15,925
Defeated the ones who fought
the Turks!

855
01:29:16,065 --> 01:29:17,925
What did Osman Bey do?

856
01:29:17,985 --> 01:29:21,585
He destroyed Geyhatu and Alemşah!

857
01:29:22,285 --> 01:29:24,005
Mashallah!

858
01:29:49,255 --> 01:29:50,535
O' people!

859
01:29:53,155 --> 01:29:58,855
We fulfilled our promise.
Thank Allah.

860
01:30:01,855 --> 01:30:04,835
These two haunted who were
trouble for the Turks...

861
01:30:10,765 --> 01:30:12,375
are in front of you now.

862
01:30:17,075 --> 01:30:18,615
One from outside...

863
01:30:22,825 --> 01:30:24,095
the other...

864
01:30:27,645 --> 01:30:29,725
the other is one of us.

865
01:30:33,915 --> 01:30:38,255
But now, they are under my sword
of justice now.

866
01:30:38,335 --> 01:30:50,925
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

867
01:30:56,045 --> 01:31:03,045
Now, take Geyhatu and Vizier Alemşah
to my tent.

868
01:31:05,785 --> 01:31:07,875
Before they breathe for the last time...

869
01:31:09,535 --> 01:31:11,295
I have things to say.

870
01:31:47,395 --> 01:31:49,455
Don't worry!

871
01:31:51,655 --> 01:31:54,025
They won't die so easily.

872
01:31:55,705 --> 01:31:57,085
But...

873
01:31:57,765 --> 01:32:00,075
but there are things we need
to find out.

874
01:32:01,655 --> 01:32:05,655
Who is Vizier Alemşah working with?

875
01:32:06,405 --> 01:32:08,145
We need to learn this.

876
01:32:09,605 --> 01:32:11,105
After then...

877
01:32:13,255 --> 01:32:15,295
I'll behead them both.

878
01:32:19,775 --> 01:32:21,305
When Geyhatu dies...

879
01:32:22,035 --> 01:32:25,185
there will be incomers from
Turkmen tribes.

880
01:32:27,825 --> 01:32:29,165
Then...

881
01:32:29,865 --> 01:32:35,515
this state that we'll foun for
the order of the world will born here.

882
01:32:36,065 --> 01:32:57,655
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

883
01:33:01,235 --> 01:33:02,765
Mother Selcan!

884
01:33:03,105 --> 01:33:04,885
Mother Selcan, help!

885
01:33:04,915 --> 01:33:06,255
Mother Selcan, help!

886
01:33:06,255 --> 01:33:08,815
-What is it?
-Orhan has a fever.

887
01:33:08,925 --> 01:33:10,725
What are you saying, my daughter?

888
01:33:11,165 --> 01:33:13,795
Bala! Stay with Alahaddin.

889
01:33:15,215 --> 01:33:17,225
Selvi, Bala is a new mother.

890
01:33:17,225 --> 01:33:19,295
Don't leave her.

891
01:33:57,715 --> 01:34:00,795
A border bey's mission is obvious.

892
01:34:02,245 --> 01:34:06,175
It's becoming a wall and
protecting the lands.

893
01:34:06,725 --> 01:34:11,585
When you find an opportunity,
it's raiding the enemy.

894
01:34:11,785 --> 01:34:14,845
It's not stabbing your sultan
on the back!

895
01:34:15,465 --> 01:34:18,195
You have done such a treachery,
Osman...

896
01:34:19,925 --> 01:34:22,115
death is an escape for you.

897
01:34:23,375 --> 01:34:28,405
Now, you have no place in Seljuk lands.

898
01:34:36,105 --> 01:34:44,675
You will be dragged after horses but
won't die, Osman!

899
01:34:44,925 --> 01:34:50,935
All the revolter tribes will take
example from you!

900
01:34:53,695 --> 01:34:57,285
Will your emperor sit after
you rebel?

901
01:34:58,565 --> 01:35:00,655
I'm coming, Osman.
I'm coming.

902
01:35:01,075 --> 01:35:04,355
I'm coming to make you pay
for your treachery.

903
01:35:05,765 --> 01:35:08,935
Orhan, what happened to you,
my child?

904
01:35:09,875 --> 01:35:11,915
You are burning.

905
01:35:12,715 --> 01:35:14,255
Alright.
Alright.

906
01:35:14,255 --> 01:35:16,895
You are burning, my child.

907
01:35:19,645 --> 01:35:20,985
My Orhan.

908
01:35:21,205 --> 01:35:23,525
Malhun?
Is Orhan alright?

909
01:35:24,105 --> 01:35:27,185
Mother, my child is burning!

910
01:35:27,395 --> 01:35:28,935
I can't lower his fewer.

911
01:35:28,935 --> 01:35:30,855
Alright.
Alright.

912
01:35:31,395 --> 01:35:32,565
What will we do, mother?

913
01:35:33,055 --> 01:35:34,565
He is burning!

914
01:35:34,565 --> 01:35:36,825
Alaca, prepare water with vinegar.

915
01:35:36,825 --> 01:35:38,155
Come on.

916
01:35:38,495 --> 01:35:40,225
Alaca, hurry!

917
01:35:44,425 --> 01:35:47,055
Alright, my child.
Alright.

918
01:35:47,385 --> 01:35:48,685
Alright.

919
01:35:49,895 --> 01:35:53,935
May Allah protect you.

920
01:36:00,975 --> 01:36:03,205
Mother, does his fewer go down?

921
01:36:03,375 --> 01:36:06,285
He is a child, my daughter.
Of course, he'll have a fever.

922
01:36:13,645 --> 01:36:14,945
My child.

923
01:36:15,175 --> 01:36:19,345
Don't cry, my baby.

924
01:36:22,385 --> 01:36:25,125
Allah is healing.
Allah is healing.

925
01:36:31,965 --> 01:36:33,445
This won't do.

926
01:36:33,615 --> 01:36:36,135
Ayşe, go and prepare
soft water...

927
01:36:36,395 --> 01:36:37,945
for Orhan.

928
01:36:37,945 --> 01:36:39,265
Alright.

929
01:36:41,405 --> 01:36:44,085
Orhan, my child!
My child!

930
01:36:44,585 --> 01:36:45,915
Malhun, strip him.

931
01:36:51,285 --> 01:36:53,815
Kervansarai on the Road

932
01:36:58,975 --> 01:37:01,065
You did well, Barkın.

933
01:37:01,355 --> 01:37:03,385
The borders are saved from
another trouble.

934
01:37:04,095 --> 01:37:06,105
Ihvaz is next.

935
01:37:35,605 --> 01:37:36,915
Is it not enough, Barkın?

936
01:37:39,375 --> 01:37:41,405
What are you doing, idiot?

937
01:37:52,685 --> 01:37:54,695
Are you afraid of me?

938
01:37:54,695 --> 01:37:56,735
Why should I?

939
01:37:58,115 --> 01:37:59,455
You will be.

940
01:37:59,945 --> 01:38:03,155
I'll make you pay for
this, Barkın!

941
01:38:03,505 --> 01:38:06,725
I spare your life against your
insult.

942
01:38:07,725 --> 01:38:10,275
Will you make me pay
for two alps?

943
01:38:10,365 --> 01:38:12,255
What insult?

944
01:38:12,385 --> 01:38:14,405
Did I kill Umur for gold?

945
01:38:15,675 --> 01:38:17,385
You can't buy me!

946
01:38:18,085 --> 01:38:19,855
You can't rule me!

947
01:38:23,065 --> 01:38:24,575
Are you afraid?

948
01:38:34,975 --> 01:38:38,975
Send my regards to Vizier Alemşah
and your brother.

949
01:38:38,975 --> 01:38:42,275
I'll visit them both soon.

950
01:38:43,865 --> 01:38:47,875
What happened will be
our secret.

951
01:39:50,345 --> 01:39:52,515
You are so coward that...

952
01:39:56,035 --> 01:39:58,305
you can't go around without
an armor.

953
01:40:00,495 --> 01:40:01,805
You are afraid...

954
01:40:03,585 --> 01:40:07,465
that your dark soul will
leave your weak body.

955
01:40:14,785 --> 01:40:15,875
Geyhatu.

956
01:40:19,805 --> 01:40:23,325
See how coward your
partner is.

957
01:40:35,455 --> 01:40:38,495
Osman will die, Gündüz.

958
01:40:40,875 --> 01:40:42,365
But you...

959
01:40:43,955 --> 01:40:48,275
you will pay dearly
for your treason.

960
01:40:50,975 --> 01:40:52,175
Thank Allah.

961
01:40:53,475 --> 01:40:55,575
Thank Allah, we returned from our mistake.

962
01:40:56,455 --> 01:40:59,535
But this won't be your option.

963
01:41:04,685 --> 01:41:08,425
Do what you will, Osman.

964
01:41:09,965 --> 01:41:13,645
Kill me if you want...

965
01:41:15,015 --> 01:41:19,305
speak if you want.

966
01:41:20,315 --> 01:41:21,645
Not me.

967
01:41:24,175 --> 01:41:25,705
Nikola will do that.

968
01:41:30,135 --> 01:41:33,495
He'll tell the dagger
you pulled against each other.

969
01:41:35,805 --> 01:41:37,375
I'll be honored.

970
01:41:43,975 --> 01:41:47,855
This Vizier Alemşah is a funny man!

971
01:41:50,695 --> 01:41:52,685
Oh, Geyhatu...

972
01:41:53,695 --> 01:41:55,605
Geyhatu the wise.

973
01:41:58,615 --> 01:42:02,365
If you heard what Vizier Alemşah
said about you...

974
01:42:02,625 --> 01:42:04,845
which you will hear soon.

975
01:42:14,605 --> 01:42:15,965
This vizier...

976
01:42:16,925 --> 01:42:19,395
came to my castle.

977
01:42:22,375 --> 01:42:23,755
Nikola, he said...

978
01:42:24,305 --> 01:42:28,245
I'll erase this barbarian Geyhatu
from these lands...

979
01:42:29,025 --> 01:42:31,255
I'll gather all the lords...

980
01:42:31,885 --> 01:42:35,255
and banish him from here,
forever!

981
01:42:39,355 --> 01:42:41,085
Shut up, Nikola!

982
01:42:41,575 --> 01:42:45,755
Stop poisoning Geyhatu with
your lies.

983
01:42:52,175 --> 01:42:55,315
Vizier Alemşah!

984
01:42:56,915 --> 01:42:58,445
Give the devil his due!

985
01:42:58,935 --> 01:43:02,155
I'm a good liar but...

986
01:43:02,655 --> 01:43:07,455
Vizier Alemşah, there is much that
I can learn from you.

987
01:43:11,765 --> 01:43:17,815
I mean, building this alliance for
too long and not revealing this?

988
01:43:18,485 --> 01:43:20,065
Right?

989
01:43:28,755 --> 01:43:30,315
My only wish...

990
01:43:32,115 --> 01:43:34,245
was a just order.

991
01:43:36,445 --> 01:43:41,175
To bring stability to these lands.

992
01:43:42,465 --> 01:43:45,565
You don't have what it
takes to do that.

993
01:43:48,135 --> 01:43:52,495
With a good way or
an evil way...

994
01:43:53,195 --> 01:43:54,995
that's all I wanted.

995
01:43:58,185 --> 01:44:02,565
Vizier...
Vizier...

996
01:44:03,775 --> 01:44:05,915
You are like a doctor who
kills.

997
01:44:19,955 --> 01:44:21,785
You love power.

998
01:44:25,255 --> 01:44:26,575
But I...

999
01:44:28,295 --> 01:44:30,745
I took your power.

1000
01:44:44,865 --> 01:44:46,205
And now...

1001
01:44:49,165 --> 01:44:51,535
you are trying to survive...

1002
01:44:55,465 --> 01:44:58,355
but I'll take your soul out.

1003
01:45:08,585 --> 01:45:09,885
Alemşah!

1004
01:45:12,485 --> 01:45:14,985
You said that in your order...

1005
01:45:14,985 --> 01:45:17,775
only the ones who can kneel
will stand.

1006
01:45:19,585 --> 01:45:20,935
Is this what you mean?

1007
01:45:21,275 --> 01:45:25,345
You would profit the most, Gündüz.

1008
01:45:26,095 --> 01:45:32,415
But now, you won't even have
a tent to sleep in.

1009
01:45:33,815 --> 01:45:37,935
I'll raze your tribe.

1010
01:45:48,395 --> 01:45:51,325
My brother and Nikola would profit, huh?

1011
01:45:55,505 --> 01:45:59,055
What about the flying fire that you
brought to destroy the walls?

1012
01:46:02,235 --> 01:46:08,765
You were going to take what yo
want and destroy the lords and the beys.

1013
01:46:14,025 --> 01:46:19,885
Osman, will you kill me
by talking?

1014
01:46:21,065 --> 01:46:26,105
Pull your sword and end it.

1015
01:46:27,895 --> 01:46:29,595
No.

1016
01:46:37,340 --> 01:46:38,640
Geyhatu.

1017
01:46:56,985 --> 01:46:59,095
You won't die easily.

1018
01:47:02,175 --> 01:47:03,525
Firstly...

1019
01:47:06,825 --> 01:47:10,335
firstly, you'll see what this
vizier was up to.

1020
01:47:13,645 --> 01:47:17,305
Then, you'll hear his suffering.

1021
01:47:20,385 --> 01:47:22,285
You made people suffer.

1022
01:47:24,785 --> 01:47:28,015
You won't die before suffering.

1023
01:47:33,645 --> 01:47:36,525
Who poisoned your warriors?

1024
01:47:37,905 --> 01:47:40,575
Who attacked you apart from us?

1025
01:47:56,385 --> 01:47:59,435
Attack!

1026
01:48:04,285 --> 01:48:09,445
If not you? Who, Osman?
Who?

1027
01:48:27,005 --> 01:48:29,035
Thank Allah, he is better.

1028
01:48:29,035 --> 01:48:31,035
The milk did him good.

1029
01:48:31,675 --> 01:48:33,185
Thank Allah.

1030
01:48:33,225 --> 01:48:34,985
He got tired from crying.

1031
01:48:36,685 --> 01:48:38,945
He sleeps so well.
Mashallah.

1032
01:48:39,005 --> 01:48:40,765
Mashallah to my brave.

1033
01:48:44,905 --> 01:48:46,265
Ayşe.

1034
01:48:46,325 --> 01:48:48,415
In the name of Allah.

1035
01:48:48,485 --> 01:48:50,065
Come on, my girl.

1036
01:48:50,075 --> 01:48:53,655
Mother. Ayşe Hatun.
Thank you.

1037
01:48:55,025 --> 01:48:57,245
Sit with your child, my girl.

1038
01:49:09,855 --> 01:49:12,975
Mother's precious.
My baby.

1039
01:49:13,835 --> 01:49:16,715
Oh, my Orhan.
You made me scared.

1040
01:49:17,375 --> 01:49:19,415
May Allah bless you.

1041
01:49:19,415 --> 01:49:21,845
May Allah protect you.
My dear son.

1042
01:49:23,495 --> 01:49:26,725
Soon, my Orhan.
Your grandfather will come.

1043
01:49:28,325 --> 01:49:31,015
Are you being shy because
of your grandfather?

1044
01:49:32,425 --> 01:49:34,695
See, he'll love you so much!

1045
01:49:38,325 --> 01:49:41,885
Oh, oh!
Great Umur Bey!

1046
01:49:42,605 --> 01:49:46,165
Who is more of a wolf than a wolf,
brave Umur Bey!

1047
01:49:50,795 --> 01:49:54,305
Many weasels tried to bite
your grandfather but...

1048
01:49:54,695 --> 01:49:57,235
he broke their fangs with
his hands.

1049
01:49:58,715 --> 01:50:02,025
Even the ones who set traps to
sow discord among your father and I...

1050
01:50:02,845 --> 01:50:04,845
were destroyed by him.

1051
01:50:04,955 --> 01:50:08,365
Your grandfather is mighty like that!

1052
01:50:16,325 --> 01:50:18,595
The one who poisoned your warriors...

1053
01:50:22,655 --> 01:50:25,165
is someone who works with Alemşah.

1054
01:50:44,585 --> 01:50:46,855
You came there.

1055
01:50:51,645 --> 01:50:53,935
How did you know it?

1056
01:51:04,925 --> 01:51:06,315
How?

1057
01:51:09,385 --> 01:51:10,725
How?

1058
01:51:23,915 --> 01:51:27,095
How did you know it?

1059
01:51:39,535 --> 01:51:40,835
Get him up.

1060
01:51:56,475 --> 01:51:58,225
Take them away.

1061
01:52:00,145 --> 01:52:01,465
This vizier...

1062
01:52:04,595 --> 01:52:06,675
will await his death now.

1063
01:52:10,585 --> 01:52:12,625
I'll talk to Geyhatu personally.

1064
01:52:30,705 --> 01:52:32,295
Now...

1065
01:52:35,205 --> 01:52:37,925
I sowed discord among them.

1066
01:52:56,285 --> 01:52:58,985
To survive, they'll sell each other out.

1067
01:53:02,075 --> 01:53:05,375
Finally, victory is ours.

1068
01:53:07,205 --> 01:53:11,735
Your part in it is doubtful, Nikola.

1069
01:53:13,675 --> 01:53:15,615
If you mean the war...

1070
01:53:16,275 --> 01:53:18,765
I retreated to
gather strength.

1071
01:53:20,605 --> 01:53:25,085
For that, my part might be a little
bigger than yours.

1072
01:53:25,785 --> 01:53:27,355
And also...

1073
01:53:27,445 --> 01:53:33,715
I'm grateful that you didn't ashame
me against the emperor.

1074
01:53:35,335 --> 01:53:38,035
Those who stand with us
don't get ashamed, Nikola.

1075
01:53:39,305 --> 01:53:41,365
Let him know that...

1076
01:53:42,275 --> 01:53:45,865
the danger is over but you couldn't
get rid of a Turkish bey.

1077
01:54:01,265 --> 01:54:05,555
Vizier Alemşah, Geyhatu...

1078
01:54:11,265 --> 01:54:15,605
Osman's enemies are dissappearing
one by one, Kosses.

1079
01:54:16,615 --> 01:54:18,815
That's what we wanted, Nikola.

1080
01:54:20,105 --> 01:54:22,165
Was it really, Kosses?

1081
01:54:22,875 --> 01:54:26,245
Osman used us and captured
all his enemies.

1082
01:54:28,405 --> 01:54:30,125
Who's turn is it now, Kosses?

1083
01:54:33,385 --> 01:54:35,175
You know it too.

1084
01:54:35,965 --> 01:54:37,745
It's our turn.

1085
01:54:40,545 --> 01:54:42,635
He'll turn to our castles first.

1086
01:54:43,635 --> 01:54:45,135
Then...

1087
01:54:46,215 --> 01:54:47,745
he'll attack us.

1088
01:54:53,515 --> 01:54:55,245
If I go now...

1089
01:54:56,635 --> 01:54:58,475
and tell Osman...

1090
01:55:02,585 --> 01:55:05,095
and he cuts you...

1091
01:55:08,315 --> 01:55:11,045
I would feel so good.

1092
01:55:14,575 --> 01:55:17,635
And I would be protecting
my castle too.

1093
01:55:19,425 --> 01:55:21,155
One stone, two birds.

1094
01:55:37,405 --> 01:55:39,155
Tell me, Geyhatu.

1095
01:55:40,445 --> 01:55:44,865
How I will kill you?

1096
01:55:46,935 --> 01:55:48,985
I heard that a lot.

1097
01:55:50,785 --> 01:55:52,805
What I want to hear...

1098
01:55:54,355 --> 01:55:55,645
is Argun Khan.

1099
01:55:57,625 --> 01:55:59,965
Argun will kill you Osman.

1100
01:56:01,235 --> 01:56:04,085
You wanted to protect this
little land...

1101
01:56:05,065 --> 01:56:09,575
all the tribes will burn
because of you.

1102
01:56:10,915 --> 01:56:12,455
Argun Khan...

1103
01:56:13,215 --> 01:56:17,835
sent an envoy to the west,
to the Europeans.

1104
01:56:20,585 --> 01:56:22,335
What is his goal?

1105
01:56:25,165 --> 01:56:26,715
What is it?

1106
01:56:28,485 --> 01:56:30,215
Was it a secret?

1107
01:56:33,235 --> 01:56:36,735
You are so afraid of the
Turks and Muslims...

1108
01:56:37,265 --> 01:56:41,985
for that reason, you want to
ally with the Christians.

1109
01:56:42,885 --> 01:56:47,235
So, you aren't as strong as you say.

1110
01:56:48,935 --> 01:56:52,135
These lands are easy, Osman.

1111
01:56:52,685 --> 01:56:56,715
But world domination requires
alliances.

1112
01:56:57,485 --> 01:57:03,565
Why are you working with the Emperor,
the lords?

1113
01:57:07,785 --> 01:57:13,135
You are small. You are with the small.

1114
01:57:16,265 --> 01:57:19,085
We are big, Osman.

1115
01:57:21,085 --> 01:57:24,265
Your big ally is Vizier Alemşah?

1116
01:57:26,265 --> 01:57:29,035
You don't even know who to ally.

1117
01:57:30,765 --> 01:57:32,635
His life is precious.

1118
01:57:33,565 --> 01:57:35,265
Sooner or later...

1119
01:57:36,985 --> 01:57:38,735
he'll say everything.

1120
01:57:41,365 --> 01:57:43,085
Vizier is small.

1121
01:57:45,785 --> 01:57:47,815
And so is his mind.

1122
01:57:49,535 --> 01:57:52,985
He betrayed me.

1123
01:57:54,115 --> 01:57:59,015
If you don't kill him, I will.

1124
01:58:02,015 --> 01:58:04,365
I'm big, Osman.

1125
01:58:05,415 --> 01:58:11,585
If you kill me, you'll see
how big I am, Osman.

1126
01:58:14,265 --> 01:58:15,515
You are big.

1127
01:58:17,985 --> 01:58:20,965
Is it why you are my captive?

1128
01:58:22,235 --> 01:58:25,465
I'll teach this to
all my children.

1129
01:58:29,835 --> 01:58:32,215
They shouldn't be above themselves.

1130
01:58:34,215 --> 01:58:37,585
Allah is greater than everyone.

1131
01:58:40,915 --> 01:58:43,085
Do you know Allah, Geyhatu?

1132
01:58:47,465 --> 01:58:49,385
In a moment of carelessness...

1133
01:58:50,815 --> 01:58:55,965
those you call small will
take you down.

1134
01:58:56,985 --> 01:58:59,785
I will kill you, Osman!

1135
01:59:03,315 --> 01:59:05,935
A dog can't bite a wolf.

1136
01:59:14,015 --> 01:59:18,335
When Genghis' grandchildren
hear that Geyhatu is dead...

1137
01:59:18,785 --> 01:59:24,465
they'll charge here to destroy
you and your lineage.

1138
01:59:27,665 --> 01:59:28,935
Then...

1139
01:59:30,935 --> 01:59:34,235
you'll see the dogs and
the wolves, Osman!

1140
01:59:41,985 --> 01:59:43,565
We'll see.

1141
01:59:44,885 --> 01:59:46,385
We'll see.

1142
01:59:47,465 --> 01:59:49,515
When the last tribe burns...

1143
01:59:49,515 --> 01:59:53,085
you will regret all this, Osman!

1144
01:59:53,085 --> 01:59:56,615
Regret!
Regret!

1145
01:59:56,675 --> 02:00:15,675
Brought to you by historicalfuntv.com

1146
02:00:15,885 --> 02:00:17,965
Come on.
Come on.

1147
02:00:22,815 --> 02:00:24,915
Come, brothers.
Come.

1148
02:00:29,435 --> 02:00:30,715
Come.

1149
02:00:43,365 --> 02:00:46,815
Cerkutay, what are you doing here,
brother?

1150
02:00:51,015 --> 02:00:52,435
Eat, Cerkutay, eat.

1151
02:00:56,115 --> 02:00:57,935
Leave some for us, brother.

1152
02:00:58,365 --> 02:01:01,585
I'm hungry, brother.
I'm hungry.

1153
02:01:05,185 --> 02:01:08,885
What are saying, Cerkutay?
Isn't Aygül Hatun cooking for you?

1154
02:01:13,765 --> 02:01:15,115
Brothers.

1155
02:01:16,265 --> 02:01:17,585
Marriage...

1156
02:01:19,585 --> 02:01:21,585
is harder than the wedding.

1157
02:01:31,585 --> 02:01:33,135
Brothers.

1158
02:01:35,385 --> 02:01:37,115
Keep in mind...

1159
02:01:37,615 --> 02:01:39,315
listen to me now...

1160
02:01:39,315 --> 02:01:42,565
keep in mind...

1161
02:01:45,665 --> 02:01:48,215
Take care of yourselves!

1162
02:01:48,865 --> 02:01:50,635
Aygül Hatun is waiting
for food.

1163
02:01:50,685 --> 02:01:52,435
Aygül Hatun is waiting for food.

1164
02:01:52,435 --> 02:01:53,965
Cerkutay!

1165
02:02:03,235 --> 02:02:07,265
-Salam Alaikum, alps.
-Alaikum Salam.

1166
02:02:15,115 --> 02:02:19,735
Cerkutay. I yelled at him but
he didn't look.

1167
02:02:20,265 --> 02:02:21,435
I hope it's good.

1168
02:02:21,665 --> 02:02:25,315
His trouble is great, Akça Dervish.

1169
02:02:26,965 --> 02:02:28,265
What are those?

1170
02:02:28,285 --> 02:02:32,415
Gündüz Bey sent it. It's the spoils
left from Geyhatu.

1171
02:02:33,765 --> 02:02:38,085
You fought bravely. You earned
these.

1172
02:02:39,035 --> 02:02:41,115
Thank you.

1173
02:02:44,335 --> 02:02:46,715
Your mother loves you, Orhan.

1174
02:02:47,635 --> 02:02:50,415
Never forget that.

1175
02:02:55,915 --> 02:02:57,435
Welcome, Osman.

1176
02:03:03,185 --> 02:03:06,185
My lion!

1177
02:03:06,565 --> 02:03:09,735
Come here! Come, come, come!

1178
02:03:13,435 --> 02:03:17,165
I was so afraid, Osman.
I didn't know what to do.

1179
02:03:18,465 --> 02:03:20,965
It's good that Mother Selcan arrived.

1180
02:03:21,385 --> 02:03:24,435
It's over now, Malhun.
It's over.

1181
02:03:24,635 --> 02:03:27,185
My lion is healthy.

1182
02:03:27,315 --> 02:03:31,485
Kumral Abdal said it.
It's how he'll grow up.

1183
02:03:32,915 --> 02:03:34,435
Thank Allah.

1184
02:03:37,085 --> 02:03:41,265
And his fire isn't from his body...

1185
02:03:42,335 --> 02:03:44,835
but his heart.

1186
02:03:49,365 --> 02:03:51,765
He'll be a fierce warrior.

1187
02:03:53,765 --> 02:03:58,265
His grandfather is a warrior, his father
is a warrior. Of course he will!

1188
02:04:06,565 --> 02:04:08,585
He even held the sword!

1189
02:04:24,985 --> 02:04:30,085
Our prophet, when he smelled
his grandchildren...

1190
02:04:30,815 --> 02:04:33,385
he would get the
smell of heaven, Bala.

1191
02:04:34,435 --> 02:04:38,465
Now, I know what heaven smells like.

1192
02:04:38,735 --> 02:04:40,815
I also get the same smell, my sheik.

1193
02:04:41,715 --> 02:04:45,785
Gratitude! My Allah gave me this joy.

1194
02:04:46,315 --> 02:04:50,435
Thank Allah!
Thank Allah, my daughter!

1195
02:04:51,265 --> 02:04:52,765
Now...

1196
02:04:53,435 --> 02:04:58,465
my grandchild Alahaddin Ali is
like fertile soil.

1197
02:04:59,565 --> 02:05:02,885
The seeds you will seed on him...

1198
02:05:03,235 --> 02:05:07,365
will be the fruits you'll get one day.

1199
02:05:09,515 --> 02:05:13,035
His reach is truth.

1200
02:05:13,785 --> 02:05:18,135
Science and knowledge will
be his two wings.

1201
02:05:18,665 --> 02:05:21,615
-Inshallah.
-Inshallah, my sheik.

1202
02:05:22,835 --> 02:05:25,285
He won't be alone on this road.

1203
02:05:26,635 --> 02:05:30,585
His brother Orhan will always
be with him.

1204
02:05:33,915 --> 02:05:35,315
By the way...

1205
02:05:36,035 --> 02:05:40,085
-How is our Orhan?
-His fever is gone.

1206
02:05:40,265 --> 02:05:44,485
-He made us afraid but he is good now.
-Thank Allah.

1207
02:05:49,285 --> 02:05:53,085
-May I enter, Malhun Hatun?
-Come, Alaca.

1208
02:05:57,165 --> 02:05:58,715
Is Orhan alright?

1209
02:06:00,265 --> 02:06:02,535
He is, thank Allah.
His fever is gone.

1210
02:06:02,985 --> 02:06:04,015
Thank Allah.

1211
02:06:04,265 --> 02:06:06,735
-Any news from my father?
-No, Malhun Hatun.

1212
02:06:07,265 --> 02:06:09,715
But he must be close.
He'll be here soon.

1213
02:06:09,715 --> 02:06:13,185
Stay with my Orhan and inform
me if something happens.

1214
02:06:18,265 --> 02:06:21,015
Thank Allah, your grandfather
is here, my Orhan.

1215
02:06:22,335 --> 02:06:24,435
Thank Allah!

1216
02:07:48,685 --> 02:07:51,735
-Father!
-Umur Bey...

1217
02:08:06,015 --> 02:08:07,335
No...

1218
02:08:32,615 --> 02:08:34,135
Uncle!

1219
02:08:37,035 --> 02:08:38,615
Umur Bey!

1220
02:08:52,635 --> 02:08:55,885
We are in this world as subjects.
Surely, we'll return to him.

1221
02:09:19,775 --> 02:09:21,155
Father.

1222
02:09:21,185 --> 02:09:23,185
What happened to you, father?

1223
02:09:24,385 --> 02:09:26,135
What happened to you?

1224
02:09:30,865 --> 02:09:33,365
Seeing you like this...

1225
02:09:34,715 --> 02:09:38,015
Is this how you come to
see your grandchild?

1226
02:10:07,035 --> 02:10:10,965
Barkin! What happened to my uncle?

1227
02:10:11,485 --> 02:10:15,135
Who did this to my uncle, Barkin?

1228
02:10:18,185 --> 02:10:21,035
Speak, Barkin!
Who did this?

1229
02:10:28,835 --> 02:10:31,965
What's happening?
Who did this?

1230
02:10:32,635 --> 02:10:34,115
Tell me!

1231
02:10:38,035 --> 02:10:41,715
We were ambushed, my Bey.
Mongols attacked.

1232
02:10:46,335 --> 02:10:50,185
We tried to defeat them, but
they were crowded.

1233
02:10:59,535 --> 02:11:01,925
Kizil Bey's son Umur Bey.

1234
02:11:03,205 --> 02:11:07,055
You set your heart to die in battle field.

1235
02:11:08,245 --> 02:11:11,045
Your prayers came true, father.

1236
02:11:12,645 --> 02:11:14,795
Your prayers came true.

1237
02:11:16,625 --> 02:11:18,885
May your shahada be blessed.

1238
02:11:37,325 --> 02:11:39,815
I am not to cry!

1239
02:11:41,585 --> 02:11:43,675
Our condolences, Malhun Hatun.

1240
02:11:43,825 --> 02:11:45,875
May his shahada be blessed.

1241
02:11:46,475 --> 02:11:49,365
May Hadrat Hamza accompany him
in the afterlife.

1242
02:11:54,835 --> 02:11:56,005
Amin.

1243
02:11:58,495 --> 02:12:00,675
Our condolences, Malhun Hatun.

1244
02:12:00,975 --> 02:12:02,845
May his shahada be blessed.

1245
02:12:02,845 --> 02:12:04,165
Amen.

1246
02:12:07,265 --> 02:12:08,785
Don't talk!

1247
02:12:11,285 --> 02:12:12,675
Don't cry!

1248
02:12:12,825 --> 02:12:15,335
Never cry after a martyr!

1249
02:12:18,085 --> 02:12:20,645
My father has met shahada.

1250
02:12:20,895 --> 02:12:23,485
His prayers he prayed all his life
came true.

1251
02:12:23,605 --> 02:12:25,325
No one is to cry!

1252
02:12:30,225 --> 02:12:32,425
Bring me those two dogs!

1253
02:12:33,485 --> 02:12:35,005
Yes my Bey.

1254
02:12:35,095 --> 02:12:36,965
Baysungur, come on.

1255
02:13:03,455 --> 02:13:05,205
Take his body inside.

1256
02:13:43,095 --> 02:13:44,625
Malhun.

1257
02:14:55,215 --> 02:14:56,565
Traitors!

1258
02:15:33,605 --> 02:15:36,765
You had the power.

1259
02:15:39,005 --> 02:15:41,685
But you didn't use it in the right way.

1260
02:15:44,915 --> 02:15:46,825
You paved the way for...

1261
02:15:48,595 --> 02:15:51,435
...cruelty all around the world!

1262
02:15:53,475 --> 02:15:59,815
You have taken many innocents'
and my alps' lives!

1263
02:16:08,525 --> 02:16:10,745
Now it is time.

1264
02:16:18,435 --> 02:16:19,585
Osman.

1265
02:16:20,815 --> 02:16:24,855
Argun will erase you from history
if you kill us.

1266
02:16:28,455 --> 02:16:30,705
If you kill me...

1267
02:16:31,245 --> 02:16:33,985
...you are not going
to be acquitted, Osman.

1268
02:16:35,004 --> 02:16:39,665
Do not be a fool because of your pain.

1269
02:17:26,455 --> 02:17:28,263
Sultan is coming!

1270
02:17:28,263 --> 02:17:31,995
Sultan Mesut is coming!

1271
02:17:31,995 --> 02:17:34,245
Sultan is coming!

1272
02:18:36,584 --> 02:18:39,555
What are you going to do now, Osman?

1273
02:18:42,985 --> 02:18:51,545
You can't dare to kill us
in front of Sultan.

1274
02:18:52,195 --> 02:18:54,254
You are not that brave.

1275
02:19:01,805 --> 02:19:03,945
Mesut will not permit.

1276
02:19:05,745 --> 02:19:09,805
You should have killed us when you
had the chance, Osman.

1277
02:19:30,205 --> 02:19:31,725
My Sultan.

1278
02:19:43,245 --> 02:19:45,325
What is happening, Osman Bey?

1279
02:19:45,825 --> 02:19:48,665
Are you going to kill Commander Geyhatu...

1280
02:19:49,305 --> 02:19:54,635
...after intending to kill me?

1281
02:19:57,005 --> 02:20:01,105
Are you going to kill Alemshah,
Vizier of the state?

1282
02:20:06,125 --> 02:20:09,655
Does your rebellion have a limit at all?

1283
02:20:12,255 --> 02:20:14,855
Hadrat Sultan Mesut.

1284
02:20:17,675 --> 02:20:20,775
I told you about everything...

1285
02:20:21,135 --> 02:20:23,925
...before the spy of those two dogs
hit you.

1286
02:20:26,865 --> 02:20:31,925
They were standing with you
in order just to continue their betrayal.

1287
02:20:36,025 --> 02:20:38,165
However, it is apparent that...

1288
02:20:39,985 --> 02:20:43,475
...my words have not influenced you.

1289
02:20:45,665 --> 02:20:48,165
Do you want me to believe your lies...

1290
02:20:48,705 --> 02:20:50,795
...or believe what I see with my own eyes?

1291
02:20:52,965 --> 02:20:55,105
Explain it all now!

1292
02:21:06,075 --> 02:21:08,395
You sided with Lords...

1293
02:21:09,495 --> 02:21:11,545
...and had an agreement with the Emperor.

1294
02:21:17,185 --> 02:21:18,905
- My Sultan...
- Enough!

1295
02:21:22,965 --> 02:21:25,245
Release Geyhatu and Vizier!

1296
02:21:27,515 --> 02:21:30,745
You are going to be judged in Konya!

1297
02:21:41,115 --> 02:21:42,405
My Sultan.

1298
